('0903ced2-c07d-4bb0-803a-0ac5b4cf2854', 'Walking Shoulder Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Walking Shoulder Tap is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '88311201', '88311201-Walking-Shoulder-Tap-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking Shoulder Tap. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Walking Shoulder Tap', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0908b422-247c-4ab7-9498-b8dfcde5914b', 'Shin Box Pigeon', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Target your hips with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79131201', '79131201-Shin-Box-Pigeon-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Move into the stretch position for Shin Box Pigeon. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 50, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Shin Box Pigeon', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09249d6e-8c33-42f9-a7af-a4ca03bf7a63', 'Donkey Diagonal Kickback (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67421201', '67421201-Cable-Donkey-Diagonal-Kickback-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Donkey Diagonal Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Donkey Diagonal Kickback', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('092de1c8-8067-48d5-8ad9-288af89ad716', 'Swing To Goblet Squat (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '75481201', '75481201-Kettlebell-Swing-to-Goblet-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Swing To Goblet Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Swing To Goblet Squat', 'squat, front_squat, lunge', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('093805a9-5d3c-4379-96c9-fc7b5ccf740d', 'Overhead Triceps Extension (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '41391201', '41391201-Band-Overhead-Triceps-Extension-(VERSION-2)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('093873fe-4247-404f-b7ac-9f6b00723db7', 'Goblet Forward Backward Lunge (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Goblet Forward Backward Lunge (version is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '86441201', '86441201-Kettlebell-Goblet-Forward-Backward-Lunge-(VERSION-.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Goblet Forward Backward Lunge (version. 2. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Forward Backward Lunge', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('094c3407-e44b-4dc7-90eb-fe3026e19bf5', 'Hip Adduction - Side Raise (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your adductors. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '10351201', '10351201-Lever-Side-Hip-Adduction_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Side Hip Adduction. 2. Set up in the starting position for Lever Side Hip Adduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your adductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Lever Side Hip Adduction', 'hip_abduction, squat, lunge', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('094dd2ab-09f9-4d88-b29a-3271b4dab20a', 'Plank Pass Through Push Up (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this pushing movement that works your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '93411201', '93411201-Dumbbell-Plank-Pass-Through-Push-up_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Plank Pass Through Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pass_through', 'Plank Pass Through Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0956010c-95da-4ec1-9b3a-1b73ac62e7a8', 'Standing Hand Behind Side Bend', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Standing Hand Behind Side Bend, focusing on your abs. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '86241201', '86241201-Standing-Hand-Behind-Side-Bend-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Hand Behind Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Standing Hand Behind Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('095ea6b8-53d2-4467-b967-7b8755ea6a0f', 'Weighted Hip Thrust', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this thrusting movement that emphasizes the glutes. The hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '27541201', '27541201-Weighted-Hip-Thrusts-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Weighted Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0964a0c1-666c-40e0-9877-f544e7662014', 'Marching On Spot Arms Swing', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Enhance your stamina and burn calories with this effective cardio movement. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '98501201', '98501201-Marching-On-Spot-Arms-Swing-(male)_Cardio_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Marching On Spot Arms Swing', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('096b4f60-2c37-44b6-8752-b184b0fdc442', 'Split Stance Horizontal Pallof Press (Cable)', 'Core', 'Cables', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Cable Split Stance Horizontal Pallof Press, focusing on your core. Your obliques work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '41061201', '41061201-Cable-Split-Stance-Horizontal-Pallof-Press-(male)_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Split Stance Horizontal Pallof Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Cable Split Stance Horizontal Pallof Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pallof_press', 'Split Stance Horizontal Pallof Press', 'woodchop, plank, dead_bug', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('096c206b-a5ba-4ea4-974b-aa4e681aef3b', 'Seated Shoulders Tap', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Seated Shoulders Tap is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '65651201', '65651201-Seated-Shoulders-Tap-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Shoulders Tap. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Shoulders Tap', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('097c1692-d25a-487e-a886-3ad67d737927', 'Walking (Treadmill)', 'Legs', 'Treadmill', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '22601201', '22601201-Walking-on-Treadmill_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walking On Treadmill. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'treadmill', 'Walking On Treadmill', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09803738-752a-4390-81bc-67480817d51d', 'Swing Back', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this swinging movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '51111201', '51111201-Swing-Back-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 2. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 3. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Swing Back', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('099d91a6-1601-4269-bdb2-d174d88ca61f', 'Side Kick Burpee', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Quads","Core"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. The chest, quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '71211201', '71211201-Side-Kick-Burpee-(female)_HIIT_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Squat down and place hands on the floor, jump feet back to plank. 2. Jump feet back toward hands, then explosively jump up with arms overhead. 3. Land softly and immediately begin the next rep. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'burpee', 'Side Kick Burpee', 'mountain_climber, box_jump, jumping_jack', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09a1e275-0ddf-4f7e-b433-cb35908745a7', 'Bear Walk', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '55401201', '55401201-Bear-Walk-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bear Walk. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Bear Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09b1bcc2-1b80-40b1-bf83-65c81d8d2645', 'Single Arm Scapular Push Up To Rotation', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your chest area and enhance overall flexibility. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '78881201', '78881201-Single-Arm-Scapular-Push-up-to-Rotation-(female)_S.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Single Arm Scapular Push Up To Rotation', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09b71a61-b529-4cce-8980-7096d544352f', 'Swipe Butt Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic kicking movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '71891201', '71891201-Swipe-Butt-Kick-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Swipe Butt Kick. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Swipe Butt Kick', 'high_knees, jumping_jack, running', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09bad5c5-6191-442c-980b-f188d1038f5c', 'Single Leg Plank (TRX)', 'Legs', 'TRX', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '11351201', '11351201-Suspender-Single-Leg-Plank-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Single Leg Plank. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Suspender Single Leg Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'trx', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('09bc9212-6193-4c36-b146-1c6623d83f5c', 'Face Down Lying Shoulder Press (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '41251201', '41251201-Dumbbell-Face-Down-Lying-Shoulder-Press-(male)_Sho.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Face Down Lying Shoulder Press. 2. Lie face down with your body in a straight line. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Face Down Lying Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('09bcf7b6-a276-4165-852d-26a6025d2058', 'Kickback (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '17341201', '17341201-Dumbbell-Kickbacks-on-Exercise-Ball_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Kickbacks On Exercise Ball. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 54, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Kickback On Exercise Ball', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('09c36146-b69c-4639-add3-199fa5e66db1', 'Happy Baby Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Happy Baby Pose provides a deep stretch for your hips, ideal for recovery and mobility work. You''ll also feel your lower back, adductors working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '67151201', '67151201-Happy-Baby-Pose-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Happy Baby Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Happy Baby Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09cbdd8b-3ebe-4cc1-8160-aeea0ba5012e', 'Kneeling Wrist Flexor Stretch', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this stretching exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '5611201', '05611201-Kneeling-Wrist-Flexor-Stretch-(female)_Forearms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Wrist Flexor Stretch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_stretch', 'Kneeling Wrist Flexor Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09df737e-5530-437d-8bef-915833e499c7', 'Side Lying Single Leg Adduction Hold', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your adductors, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '79781201', '79781201-Side-Lying-Single-Leg-Adduction-Hold-(female)_Stre.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Move into the stretch position for Side Lying Single Leg Adduction Hold. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time. 6. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. 7. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 40, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Side Lying Single Leg Adduction Hold', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09e990ae-674f-4a21-b378-baf7886771e5', 'Overhead Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57231201', '57231201-Bodyweight-Overhead-Squat-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. An effective movement for your legs routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Overhead Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09ed8f78-4da4-4230-90b5-cf5d0e34a244', 'Standing Mid Air Finger Bounces', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Mid Air Finger Bounces is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '65931201', '65931201-Standing-Mid-Air-Finger-Bounces-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Mid Air Finger Bounces. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Standing Mid Air Finger Bounces', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('09fa298a-1258-463e-9192-54e101b8ea03', 'Lat Stretch (Against Wall)', 'Back', 'Wall', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Target your lats with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '95331201', '95331201-Lat-Stretch-against-Wall-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.603963+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lat Stretch Against Wall. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 32, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Lat Stretch Against Wall', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a0c3dcf-b5ee-44f4-9f50-cfe2ad51a4f9', 'Side Lunge Rock', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '80671201', '80671201-Side-Lunge-Rock-(beginner)-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Step to the side, bending that knee while keeping the other leg straight. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Side Lunge Rock', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a1e5b79-1ad1-48ef-a4bf-6222032c51f5', 'Knee To Chest Stretch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '5591201', '05591201-Knee-to-Chest-Stretch-(female)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Knee To Chest Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Knee To Chest Stretch', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a22ee98-8d52-41e0-bf45-36bd9741cab2', 'Shoulder Press - Reverse Grip (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '87961201', '87961201-Lever-Reverse-Seated-Shoulder-Press_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Reverse Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Lever Reverse Seated Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0a289afa-2cd6-4d80-9dfe-85fa06ffdadd', 'Lying Triceps Extension (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lying Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '22511201', '22511201-Dumbbell-Lying-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.914483+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying Triceps Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying Triceps Extension. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lying Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0a386a24-a633-44c6-82fc-462185b7669c', 'Inchworm', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '46621201', '46621201-Inchworm-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Inchworm. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'inchworm', 'Inchworm', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a3e60eb-9578-469d-ac24-5eb1bb7ea889', 'Kneeling Sissy Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Kneeling Sissy Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '47221201', '47221201-Bodyweight-Kneeling-Sissy-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Kneeling Sissy Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a4502b1-c1c4-43d1-92ec-4e35b4229780', 'Single Leg Squat (pistol)', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Your glutes work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '17591201', '17591201-Single-Leg-Squat-(pistol)-(male)_Thighs-FIX3_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pistol_squat', 'Single Leg Squat', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a49ca9a-7167-4595-a8f8-4269910c652b', 'Hand Swipes Side Step', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Hand Swipes Side Step builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Secondary activation of your quads provides additional muscle engagement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '79451201', '79451201-Hand-Swipes-Side-Step-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Set up in the starting position for Hand Swipes Side Step. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Hand Swipes Side Step', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a4cd44d-774a-4c0b-94a4-37a8c052f489', 'Body Up', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this movement exercise for bigger arms. Your chest work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '81021201', '81021201-Body-Up-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Body Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Body Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a56892b-dbc5-45c8-b872-cf8496a29229', 'Sideway Turn', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs. Consistency with this movement will yield noticeable results.', '78121201', '78121201-Sideway-Turn-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Sideway Turn. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Sideway Turn', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a620ee2-6311-49f5-adff-dcfe9911d01a', 'Weighted Squat Side Leg Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '105801201', '105801201-Weighted-Squat-Side-Leg-Kick-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Weighted Squat Side Leg Kick', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a648908-decc-40cc-b201-167d35fbe846', 'Bent Over Rear Deltoid Kickback (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this kicking movement focusing on your rear delts. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. The bent over position requires core engagement to maintain a neutral spine. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '87091201', '87091201-Band-Bent-Over-Rear-Deltoid-Kickback-(male)_Should.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Bent Over Rear Deltoid Kickback. 2. Hinge at your hips, pushing them back while keeping your back flat. 3. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 4. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Bent Over Rear Deltoid Kickback', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0a851f26-b48b-45ca-a27f-4b681a5a49ba', 'Hip Abduction (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'The Cable Hip Abduction is a lower body movement exercise that targets your glute med/abductors. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '8791201', '08791201-Cable-Hip-Abduction-(version-2)-(female)_Hips-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Hip Abduction. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Hip Abduction. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your glute med/abductors. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0a88e621-3f3e-4bf4-89f9-eb4b051f9fa5', 'Seated Leg Kick (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this kicking exercise for quad development. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '84301201', '84301201-Seated-Leg-Kick-on-a-Chair-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.507873+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Leg Kick On A Chair', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0a9ee600-82fd-4de8-a25c-55d29d513e33', 'Seated Dip (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Machine', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Lever Seated Dip targets your triceps through a dipping motion. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '22501201', '22501201-Lever-Seated-Dip-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Dip. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 4. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Lever Seated Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0aa0b1db-8626-4b57-a8c7-f54d63b20534', 'Incline Hammer Curl (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Incline Bench', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '68701201', '68701201-Band-Incline-Hammer-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Incline Hammer Curl. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Incline Hammer Curl', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0aa696e7-3099-40d4-ae6e-eff6c90335f5', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise On Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Seated In Out Leg Raise On Floor, focusing on your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '35091201', '35091201-Seated-In-Out-Leg-Raise-on-Floor_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Seated In Out Leg Raise On Floor. 2. Sit on the floor with your legs positioned as required. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 67, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Seated In Out Leg Raise On Floor', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0aab604b-7744-4927-b946-3c46b70e0e6a', 'Single Leg Chest Press (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Suspender One Leg Chest Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '11261201', '11261201-Suspender-One-Leg-Chest-Press-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender One Leg Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Suspender Single Leg Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('0ab4a3fd-f079-4146-916e-001ea985f4ef', 'Incline Shoulder Press (Plate Loaded Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Machine', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Lever Shoulder Press (plate Loaded) is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '8691201', '08691201-Lever-Shoulder-Press-(plate-loaded)-(VERSION-2)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Shoulder Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Lever Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0ab70a10-d830-40f3-bea0-6fb6f077814b', 'Incline Pushdown (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Incline Pushdown is a pushing exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '1721201', '01721201-Cable-Incline-Pushdown_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Pushdown. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Incline Pushdown. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your triceps. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 63, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_pushdown', 'Incline Pushdown', 'tricep_extension, close_grip_bench, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0abf8aff-9a4c-449a-8b55-53790a59d04e', 'Walk Forward And Backward', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Walk Forward And Backward is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic stepping movements. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '92621201', '92621201-Walk-Forward-and-Backward-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.91585+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Walk Forward And Backward. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Walk Forward And Backward', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ac22d98-ff50-4f76-a818-b3270f41f6c2', 'Overhead Triceps Extension - Rope (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'This extension movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '22481201', '22481201-Cable-Overhead-Triceps-Extension-(rope-attachment)-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0ac54293-ae48-4ca8-962e-bc8fa9596c31', 'Kneeling Pseudo Planche Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts, core provides additional muscle engagement. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '103901201', '103901201-Kneeling-Pseudo-Planche-Push-up_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 5, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Kneeling Pseudo Planche Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0accc6c8-1b5b-47d3-9352-192c00d65a3e', 'Narrow Chair Stand Up (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this rowing movement focusing on your upper back. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '28351201', '28351201-Cable-Narrow-Chair-Stand-Up_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.931873+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Narrow Chair Stand Up. 2. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 3. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Narrow Chair Stand Up', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0ace8b80-e043-422b-8d5a-a2833823fb2f', 'Butterfly Pull Up (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '106881201', '106881201-Butterfly-Pull-Up-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 2. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Butterfly Pull Up', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl, chin_up', TRUE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ad41cb1-b157-4baf-857c-7999ad0a70b2', 'Standing Military Press - Close Grip (Barbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Barbell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Standing Close Grip Military Press is a pressing exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. You''ll also feel your triceps working to support the movement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '30311201', '30311201-Barbell-Standing-Close-Grip-Military-Press-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Standing Close Grip Military Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 4. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 5. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 6. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 99, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'shoulder_press', 'Standing Military Press - Close Grip', 'Standing Military Press - Close Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0aef99c7-7ab1-444b-a97f-4df2b9ce2cc0', 'Lying Triceps Extension (EZ Bar)', 'Arms', 'EZ Bar, Flat Bench', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The EZ Barbell Lying Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '58731201', '58731201-EZ-Barbell-Lying-Triceps-Extension-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for EZ Barbell Lying Triceps Extension. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for EZ Barbell Lying Triceps Extension. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'EZ Lying Triceps Extension', 'EZ Lying Triceps Extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0b08f8e4-8c99-4b1a-a3bc-96fb5e36ce36', 'Kneeling Fist To Palm Switch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Fist To Palm Switch is an arm movement exercise targeting your core. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '77741201', '77741201-Kneeling-Fist-to-Palm-Switch-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Fist To Palm Switch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Kneeling Fist To Palm Switch', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b13faf7-6527-465a-803c-174e1218e0e3', 'U Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the U Squat builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '64041201', '64041201-U-Squat-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. Beneficial for overall plyometrics development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'U Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b1449cb-0df9-4d4e-b3b7-e4b1afcb0420', 'Majorette Twist Rep', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Majorette Twist Rep provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '79021201', '79021201-Majorette-Twist-Rep-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Majorette Twist Rep. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Move into the stretch position for Majorette Twist Rep. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Majorette Twist Rep', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b1e1f98-771a-4edd-9d4f-6910a5546140', 'Bicep Hold - Isometric (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your biceps, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '101401201', '101401201-Resistance-Band-Isometric-Biceps-Hold-(female)_St.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Isometric Biceps Hold. 2. Move into the stretch position for Resistance Band Isometric Biceps Hold. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Isometric Bicep Hold', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0b2b74dd-b7d8-4a4a-9e6c-7a7c5a61675b', 'Toe Tap Split Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'The Toe Tap Split Jump is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic jumping movements. You''ll also feel your quads, calves working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '69831201', '69831201-Toe-Tap-Split-Jump-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Toe Tap Split Jump. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge_jump', 'Toe Tap Split Jump', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b2bc4f1-897d-48e5-a4f2-8fa56d26bd94', 'Twisting Standing Single Arm Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '12111201', '12111201-Cable-Twisting-Standing-One-Arm-Chest-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Twisting Standing One Arm Chest Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 69, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Twisting Standing Single Arm Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0b32e9d5-15fb-45a1-add3-bece4545f6d5', 'Bent Knee Abduction Crunch With Arms Through', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '73931201', '73931201-Bent-Knee-Abduction-Crunch-with-Arms-Through-(fema.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.347577+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Bent Knee Abduction Crunch With Arms Through', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b3b7456-4105-4f58-9f79-2a0338569c8c', 'Seated Open Wings', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your core. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Quality repetitions are more important than quantity.', '89391201', '89391201-Seated-Open-Wings-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.172397+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Open Wings. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Seated Open Wings', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b412a59-48d6-4530-bc90-a03809afe58d', 'Squat Hamstring Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this curling exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '77001201', '77001201-Squat-Hamstring-Curl-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 2. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 3. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Squat Hamstring Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('0b4181b5-90bd-47e8-b450-c1e15efa1826', 'Fly (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This flying exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '57371201', '57371201-Suspension-Fly_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspension Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Suspension Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('0b669d9d-c62d-468b-8abd-47969819308b', 'Bicep Curl - Cross Chest (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '70921201', '70921201-Band-Cross-Chest-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Cross Chest Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Cross Chest Bicep Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0b70bc80-b848-45a6-8524-7328588515d6', 'Incline Hammer Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Incline Hammer Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '3211201', '03211201-Dumbbell-Incline-Hammer-Press_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Hammer Press. 2. Use a hammer/neutral grip with palms facing each other throughout. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'incline_press', 'Incline Hammer Press', 'bench_press, shoulder_press, chest_fly', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0b7898e6-236d-412f-b62f-3092fcb62ca8', 'Deep Lunge Circle', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Deep Lunge Circle is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '78991201', '78991201-Deep-Lunge-Circle-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement. This exercise is excellent for quads development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Deep Lunge Circle', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0b8da56e-14e9-43c5-8b83-449d47cd51a7', '4 Punches Side Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build total body strength and coordination with this multi-joint squatting movement. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Full body exercises are time-efficient and build functional, real-world strength.', '61111201', '61111201-4-Punches-Side-Squat-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.292204+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', '4 Punches Side Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ba2e6f3-bc4c-4d8a-9d99-f27e739100eb', 'Glute Bridge Straight Leg Open - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '97151201', '97151201-Glute-Bridge-Alternating-Straight-Leg-Open-(female.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Glute Bridge Straight Leg Open - Alternating', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ba73387-fa16-4856-8ce6-f15d71098fba', 'Reverse Lunge Quick Arms', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic lunging movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '60831201', '60831201-Reverse-Lunge-Quick-Arms-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Step backward, lowering your back knee toward the floor. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Reverse Lunge Quick Arms', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0bb17e92-17b9-4bdb-aef6-5349c55b4b0a', 'Half Jumping Jack', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Calves"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Half Jumping Jack builds reactive power and improves conditioning. You''ll also feel your shoulders, calves working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '86231201', '86231201-Half-Jumping-Jack-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Half Jumping Jack. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'jumping_jack', 'Half Jumping Jack', 'burpee, high_knees, jump_rope', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0bb2591c-0f8a-4dcb-8f55-f23171aa5c57', 'Side To Side Side Punch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this movement exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '84581201', '84581201-Side-to-Side-Side-Punch-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.429219+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side To Side Side Punch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Side To Side Side Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0bcd34c7-48ee-47ac-8e2c-10733d6544fd', 'Kneeling Single Kickback Fire Hydrant', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Single Kickback Fire Hydrant is a hip-dominant kicking exercise that targets your glutes. Your hip abductors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '65671201', '65671201-Kneeling-Single-Kickback-Fire-Hydrant-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_circle', 'Kneeling Single Kickback Fire Hydrant', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0bd8179b-a77c-4efc-867c-916a7169c0f4', 'Donkey Kickback', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Donkey Kickback is a hip-dominant kicking exercise that targets your glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '63141201', '63141201-Donkey-Kickback-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.624497+00', '1. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 2. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Donkey Kickback', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0bde1dfd-d4df-414b-a1a3-17db1b60375f', 'Seated Shoulder Waves', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '87251201', '87251201-Seated-Shoulder-Waves-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.848698+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Shoulder Waves. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Shoulder Waves', 'lateral_raise, shoulder_press, front_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0befa7b2-ba02-44cc-968e-b05902123c24', 'Seated Shoulders Press (Chair) - Alternating', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this pressing movement that works your core. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '104821201', '104821201-Seated-Alternating-Shoulders-Press-on-Chair-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.93819+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 7. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Seated Shoulders Press On Chair - Alternating', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c17e636-cc94-4b3c-8930-6d4ccafaff48', 'Kneeling Dynamic Plank', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Kneeling Dynamic Plank, focusing on your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '65781201', '65781201-Kneeling-Dynamic-Plank-(female)_Waist1_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.322534+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Kneeling Dynamic Plank', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c2525ea-73b6-488f-8e58-2bd79147229a', 'Seated Knee Thrust (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '83061201', '83061201-Seated-Knee-Thrust-on-a-Chair-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 4. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 5. Lower your hips back down with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'knee_drive', 'Seated Knee Thrust On A Chair', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c264a41-723f-4c17-bd77-5a76358df313', 'Step Out - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity stepping exercise that challenges your entire body. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '44361201', '44361201-Alternating-Step-Out_Plyometrics.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Out - Alternating', 'stretch_hip, dynamic_warmup, yoga_pose', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('0c32d7a7-1fc1-41e1-bfc0-dcebdf206a9b', 'Single Arm Row - Overhand (Machine)', 'Back', 'Machine', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '85941201', '85941201-Lever-Seated-Single-Arm-Row-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.123147+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated Single Arm Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Lever Seated Single Arm Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, bicep_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0c39e539-edb5-4f42-a548-cc72bd1e4364', 'Rear Lunge Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Rear Lunge Twist is a lunging exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '73641201', '73641201-Bodyweight-Rear-Lunge-Twist-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.36063+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Rear Lunge Twist', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c4062c5-ea14-42b1-8acf-f05c806cf8f6', 'Seated Rhomboid Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Seated Rhomboid Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '67741201', '67741201-Seated-Rhomboid-Stretch-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Rhomboid Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Rhomboid Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c421e1d-7754-420b-a559-a874cd7f1567', 'Seated Lean Forward Groin Stretch (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Seated Lean Forward Groin Stretch On A Chair provides a deep stretch for your adductors, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The hips assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '91631201', '91631201-Sitting-Lean-forward-Groin-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Lean Forward Groin Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Seated Lean Forward Groin Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c4f5e2e-2a7f-4c1a-bf10-60fbfa072071', 'Lying External Shoulder Rotation (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Lying External Shoulder Rotation is a rotation exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '83471201', '83471201-Dumbbell-Lying-External-Shoulder-Rotation-(male)_B.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Lying External Shoulder Rotation. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Dumbbell Lying External Shoulder Rotation. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Dumbbell Lying External Shoulder Rotation. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_exercise', 'Lying External Shoulder Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0c500eb7-253a-4e5d-b4b6-6f1ed592de62', 'Standing Stepback', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this stepping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. The quads assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93771201', '93771201-Standing-Stepback-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Stepback', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0c6532c8-42aa-48fa-807f-086da6d2b535', 'Hack Squat (Hack Squat Machine)', 'Legs', 'Hack Squat Machine', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes provides additional muscle engagement. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '23841201', '23841201-Sled-Hack-Squat-(female)_Thighs.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set. Perfect for targeting your quads. Variation: Sled Hack Squat.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'hack_squat', 'Sled Hack Squat', 'leg_press, squat, leg_extension', TRUE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0c6d26f9-8163-4a68-8336-e595024ff4de', 'Snatch And Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Full Body', 'Kettlebell', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Snatch And Swing is a lower body swinging exercise that targets your full body. Your quads, shoulders work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '74681201', '74681201-Kettlebell-Snatch-and-Swing-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Snatch And Swing. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'snatch', 'Snatch And Swing', 'power_snatch, clean, overhead_press', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('0c6da7fe-4118-4d52-9d73-98dbe10cc9ea', 'Garland Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '63221201', '63221201-Garland-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Garland Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hip_stretch', 'Garland Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0cabbb43-85f6-4d88-a39b-eda875221761', 'Full Front Raise Catch (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Full Front Raise Catch is a raising exercise that targets your front delts for shoulder development. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '105591201', '105591201-Dumbbell-Full-Front-Raise-Catch-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Full Front Raise Catch. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Full Front Raise Catch', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0cafc550-5035-43cc-b02c-a8bf5a2fd25d', 'Standing Shoulder Press To Pec Dec (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '86491201', '86491201-Dumbbell-Standing-Shoulder-Press-to-Pec-Dec-(male).mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Shoulder Press To Pec Dec. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 94, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Standing Shoulder Press To Pec Dec', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0cb269b4-8336-4548-9bb6-37c363766c3b', 'Seated Side Leg Lift (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '105011201', '105011201-Seated-Side-Leg-Lift-on-Chair-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.851102+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. Ideal for core strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Seated Side Leg Lift On Chair', 'crunch, plank, russian_twist, hanging_knee_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0cc0e9d9-4f46-42f8-ad7f-6fac689e397f', 'Pinch (Plate)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Biceps"}'::text[], 'The Plate Pinch is an arm movement exercise targeting your upper back. You''ll also feel your biceps working to support the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '10441201', '10441201-Plate-Pinch_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Plate Pinch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your upper back. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Plate Pinch', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0cc12108-1fd6-4651-97e6-ff8efc19710c', 'Face Pull (Band)', 'Shoulders', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'The Band Face Pull is a pulling exercise that targets your delts for shoulder development. The upper back, rotator cuff assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '56071201', '56071201-Band-Face-Pull-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.099411+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Face Pull. 2. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 3. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 4. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0cd73e62-0317-421b-ab92-d0662e4973d2', 'Goblet Marching On Spot (Kettlebell)', 'Legs', 'Kettlebell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Goblet Marching On Spot is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '75321201', '75321201-Kettlebell-Goblet-Marching-on-Spot-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.196858+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Goblet Marching On Spot. 2. Set up in the starting position for Kettlebell Goblet Marching On Spot. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 58, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Goblet Marching On Spot', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'kettlebell', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('0cdec75d-315a-425a-b696-6341b5631795', 'Side Step Back Toe Tap Walk - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic stepping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. You''ll also feel your quads working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '98341201', '98341201-Alternating-Side-Step-Back-Toe-Tap-Walk-(male)_Ply.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.805708+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Side Step Back Toe Tap Walk - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0cfd8b5a-09a9-421d-82c1-ec20ef49895b', 'Baddha Konasana Flow Pose', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Baddha Konasana Flow Pose provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '79671201', '79671201-Baddha-Konasana-Flow-Pose-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.685158+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Baddha Konasana Flow Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Baddha Konasana Flow Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d002e3d-deeb-497e-a44e-216e585fbe29', 'Elbow Plank With Single Arm Pulldo (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Resistance Band Elbow Plank With Single Arm Pulldo, focusing on your abs. The shoulders, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '76841201', '76841201-Resistance-Band-Elbow-Plank-with-Single-Arm-Pulldo.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Elbow Plank With Single Arm Pulldo. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Elbow Plank With Single Arm Pulldo', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0d063952-1830-4541-8c27-9598a9f47c2a', 'KAS Glute Bridge (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Barbell KAS Glute Bridge is a hip-dominant bridging exercise that targets your glutes. Your hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '54511201', '54511201-Barbell-KAS-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.013316+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell KAS Glute Bridge. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'KAS Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0d077e27-9620-4819-b005-cda4941db202', 'Renegade Row Walk (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Renegade Row Walk is a core rowing exercise that primarily targets your abs. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '82251201', '82251201-Dumbbell-Renegade-Row-Walk-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Renegade Row Walk. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Renegade Row Walk', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0d0af7bc-458a-4ed2-af63-e8ecc7f8e306', 'Standing Curl - Wide Grip (Barbell)', 'Arms', 'Barbell', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. You''ll also feel your forearms working to support the movement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '69901201', '69901201-Barbell-Standing-Wide-grip-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arm.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Standing Wide Grip Curl. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 84, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Standing Curl - Wide Grip', 'Standing Curl - Wide Grip', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0d12ba6f-ee27-4dcc-bf7e-dcd07376c92d', 'Seated Shoulder Press And Hip Abduction On A Padd', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Target your delts with the Seated Shoulder Press And Hip Abduction On A Padd, an effective shoulder pressing exercise. The triceps assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '56551201', '56551201-Sitting-Shoulder-Press-and-Hip-Abduction-on-a-padd.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press And Hip Abduction On A Padd', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d132dda-6bd4-4c63-8a02-27367a610e1c', 'Lying Side Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lying Side Stretch provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '52561201', '52561201-Lying-Side-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Side Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Lying Side Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d142e38-1556-4fc2-a61f-16d533a14b8b', 'Seated Row - Wide Grip (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '2181201', '02181201-Cable-Seated-Wide-grip-Row_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Wide Grip Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Use a wide grip (wider than shoulder-width) for this variation. 4. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 5. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 6. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Seated Row - Wide Grip', 'Seated Row - Wide Grip', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0d146a84-8bd5-463f-bef9-a415d0d99c92', 'Cobra To Child Pose', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your back, the Cobra To Child Pose helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The hips assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '85491201', '85491201-Cobra-to-Child-Pose-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cobra To Child Pose. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Cobra To Child Pose', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d17fc82-3737-4f81-be39-6ba250afe577', 'Incline Row (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '491201', '00491201-Barbell-Incline-Row_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.755209+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Incline Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Row', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Incline Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0d353e2b-afd4-4105-a3b0-a93edeea65a7', 'Bicep Curl (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Machine', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '74101201', '74101201-Lever-Biceps-Curl-(female)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Lever Bicep Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0d360725-902c-412b-ae1b-2d671079a72b', 'Standing Twist (Barbell)', 'Core', 'Barbell', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Standing Twist targets your obliques through a twisting motion, building rotational core strength. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '23201201', '23201201-Barbell-Standing-Twist-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Standing Twist. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Barbell Standing Twist. 4. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', 'Flexion', NULL, 'Isolation', 'Unilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, 'Overhand', 'Wide', 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Standing Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0d4026f2-3144-46e0-b600-74c1edcabb35', 'Standing Wrist Rotation', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this rotation exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '69781201', '69781201-Standing-Wrist-Rotation-(male)_Forearms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Wrist Rotation. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_stretch', 'Standing Wrist Rotation', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d411f94-0e76-4e0f-99eb-655c25eea414', 'Mid Air Lateral Raise With Switching Palms', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Mid Air Lateral Raises With Switching Palms is a raising exercise that targets your lateral delts for shoulder development. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '74291201', '74291201-Mid-Air-Lateral-Raises-With-Switching-Palms-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.532804+00', '1. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Mid Air Lateral Raise With Switching Palms', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d433491-6556-4f3b-8e7d-5e5c3950fdc8', 'Side Swing (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Kettlebell Side Swing, focusing on your abs. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '83661201', '83661201-Kettlebell-Side-Swing-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.392006+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Side Swing. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'kettlebell_swing', 'Side Swing', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('0d4b5cd0-ffce-485f-8e87-3af36829cb40', 'Elliptical Machine - Skiing (Elliptical)', 'Full Body', 'Elliptical', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build your aerobic capacity with this steady-state cardio movement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Regular cardio training builds the aerobic base for better overall fitness.', '26581201', '26581201-Elliptical-Machine-Skiing-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.505723+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Elliptical Machine Skiing. 2. Set up in the starting position for Elliptical Machine Skiing. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 2, 2, NULL, 10, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Cardio', 58, 9, 8, FALSE, TRUE, 'elliptical', 'Elliptical  Skiing', 'Elliptical Skiing', FALSE, 'machine', TRUE, 1, 60, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0d613c4e-7ef4-41e7-a99b-6f6fea30e10b', 'Forward Bend Back Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your back, the Forward Bend Back Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. You''ll also feel your shoulders working to support the movement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '67641201', '67641201-Forward-Bend-Back-Stretch-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.640031+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Forward Bend Back Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Forward Bend Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d63bb50-d522-4ef0-aa4c-b490d6c848ef', 'High Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. This variation is excellent for building mind-muscle connection.', '65031201', '65031201-Cable-High-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the highest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'High Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0d67a180-02f4-4d8d-92b2-53cebc14942d', 'Standing Front Raise (EZ Bar)', 'Shoulders', 'EZ Bar', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the EZ Bar Standing Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '55231201', '55231201-EZ-Bar-Standing-Front-Raise_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.737494+00', '1. Grip the EZ bar on the angled portions for a comfortable wrist position. 2. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 3. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'EZ Bar Standing Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'ez_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0d67d766-f85d-44dd-8a4c-22322727d156', 'Incline Y Raise With Back Support (Cable)', 'Shoulders', 'Cables', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'This raising exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Secondary activation of your upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '86611201', '86611201-Cable-Incline-Y-Raise-with-Back-Support-(male)_Sho.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.79417+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Incline Y Raise With Back Support. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Cable Incline Y Raise With Back Support. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 83, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Incline Y Raise With Back Support', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0d7a116c-3077-41d8-8c4d-9624c5d95810', 'Quick Sumo Quarter Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Inner Thighs","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This dynamic squatting movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '53231201', '53231201-Quick-Sumo-Quarter-Squat-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.936279+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. Include this in your plyometrics training.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Quick Sumo Quarter Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d8b0a32-edcc-42d0-a63f-8c5e60e0e2b0', 'Side Step Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Abs"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Crunch is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic crunching movements. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '66671201', '66671201-Side-Step-Crunch-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Side Step Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0d94c80d-efdb-4c08-99b9-77b4e50179d8', 'Kneeling Single Hamstring Curl (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Strengthen the back of your thighs with this curling exercise. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kneeling position adds a core stability challenge. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '67481201', '67481201-Kneeling-Single-Hamstring-Curl-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_curl', 'Kneeling Single Hamstring Curl', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('0da44da2-92f9-4639-8283-c51c2467b6f9', 'Incline Palm In Press (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Dumbbell Incline Palm In Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. Using an incline changes the angle of resistance for varied muscle recruitment. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '3241201', '03241201-Dumbbell-Incline-Palm-in-Press_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Incline Palm In Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Incline Palm In Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0da458d3-4af5-4ad9-8b8a-4fa6de4d8d7a', 'Decline Shrug (Barbell)', 'Back', 'Barbell, Decline Bench', '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Barbell Decline Shrug is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. Declining shifts the emphasis to hit the muscles from a different angle. Using a barbell provides stability for progressive overload. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '68141201', '68141201-Barbell-Decline-Shrug_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.203368+00', '1. Grip a barbell with hands at the appropriate width for Barbell Decline Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Decline Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0db11956-d237-45a8-ac6c-6463845b1369', 'Kneeling Side Leg To Kick', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your core. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '48131201', '48131201-Kneeling-Side-Leg-to-Kick-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Side Leg To Kick. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Side Leg To Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0dc71b55-3ef4-47b0-8c44-2c3026947de1', 'Standing Arms Swing - Alternating', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Alternating Arms Swing provides a deep stretch for your full body, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '98311201', '98311201-Standing-Alternating-Arms-Swing-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.504261+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Hinge at your hips, letting the weight swing back between your legs. 3. Explosively drive hips forward, propelling the weight forward/up. 4. Let gravity bring it back as you hinge for the next rep. 5. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'arm_exercise', 'Standing Arms Swing - Alternating', 'bicep_curl, tricep_extension, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0dc9c496-27ea-4e10-986b-c3f5308c518d', 'Kneeling Wrist Flexion Curl (Resistance Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Resistance Band Kneeling Wrist Flexion Curl is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '84721201', '84721201-Resistance-Band-Kneeling-Wrist-Flexion-Curl-(femal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Kneeling Wrist Flexion Curl. 2. Kneel on the floor (use a pad for comfort if needed). 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Kneeling Wrist Flexion Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0dd712b9-ae77-4056-898d-f7cc4ed9af05', 'Monster Walk (Resistance Band)', 'Full Body', 'Resistance Band', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stepping movement focusing on your full body. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '48091201', '48091201-Resistance-Band-Monster-Walk_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.71819+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Monster Walk. 2. Set up in the starting position for Resistance Band Monster Walk. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'walking', 'Monster Walk', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0de540c7-7c21-42d7-8668-3af365923a3b', 'Seated Shoulder Press - Parallel Grip (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '25931201', '25931201-Dumbbell-Seated-Shoulder-Press-(parallel-grip)-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.168801+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Seated Shoulder Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 4. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 5. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 86, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Seated Shoulder Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0de80493-abd5-4920-88e7-572125db9f8b', 'Zottman Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '4391201', '04391201-Dumbbell-Zottman-Curl_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.938497+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Zottman Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Zottman Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0dea0cde-7956-48b5-a814-b9395c653ae5', 'Lying Leg Raise (TRX)', 'Core', 'TRX', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Suspender Lying Leg Raise is a core raising exercise that primarily targets your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '75011201', '75011201-Suspender-Lying-Leg-Raise-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Lying Leg Raise. 2. Lie down in the appropriate position for Suspender Lying Leg Raise. 3. Keeping legs mostly straight, raise them toward the ceiling. 4. Lower with control, stopping just before touching down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Suspender Lying Leg Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('0e0412be-a23b-4437-a2c5-a11781fb6e68', 'Plank Jack', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This stabilization exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Can be modified for beginners or progressed for advanced athletes.', '46421201', '46421201-Plank-Jack-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.667316+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. An effective movement for your core routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 70, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Jack', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e14924b-808e-429e-9672-74ea32b35c54', 'Curl - Close Grip (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'This curling exercise focuses on your biceps for improved arm size and strength. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '41521201', '41521201-Dumbbell-Close-Grip-Curl_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Close Grip Curl. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Curl - Close Grip', 'Curl - Close Grip', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0e27a76c-ecf7-400b-b5bf-6791879ed4a8', 'Standing Lat Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '85881201', '85881201-Standing-Lat-Pulldown-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.7451+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Standing Lat Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0e3072f7-92f3-4d04-97d0-683d149c5ddc', 'Side Lying Side Lift Free Lateral Flexion', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This flexion exercise engages your core for improved core stability and strength. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '94061201', '94061201-Side-Lying-Side-Lift-free-Lateral-Flexion-(female).mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Side Lift Free Lateral Flexion. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Lying Side Lift Free Lateral Flexion', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e30b7ee-e076-4270-9da0-140782a002a0', 'Half Squat Side Lunge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '74891201', '74891201-Half-Squat-Side-Lunge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. Great for building strength in your quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Half Squat Side Lunge', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e31e00b-3b5b-4605-9ef1-29d062039731', 'Standing Balance Hip Abduction (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your hip abductors. The glutes assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '67361201', '67361201-Resistance-Band-Standing-Balance-Hip-Abduction-(fe.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.266593+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Standing Balance Hip Abduction. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_abduction', 'Standing Balance Hip Abduction', 'hip_adduction, glute_bridge, clamshell', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0e32d3cd-eb2b-4629-9c30-ce885c0289fe', 'Side Step Chest Fly Walk', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Side Step Chest Fly Walk is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic flying movements. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '92541201', '92541201-Side-Step-Chest-Fly-Walk-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. An effective movement for your plyometrics routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Side Step Chest Fly Walk', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e36489a-4bf5-4200-a140-d29b06b37132', 'Standing Side Bend Curtsey', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity movement exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '89281201', '89281201-Standing-Side-Bend-Curtsey-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.870314+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Side Bend Curtsey. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Standing Side Bend Curtsey', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e3eda3b-5c53-4083-812e-df886fef4d7d', 'Dead Bug (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Weighted Kettlebell Dead Bug, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '95171201', '95171201-Weighted-Kettlebell-Dead-Bug-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Weighted Kettlebell Dead Bug. 2. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Kettlebell Dead Bug. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dead_bug', 'Dead Bug', 'plank, bird_dog, hollow_hold', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('0e3eeb2b-9292-43f8-84f5-8193f5530ab9', 'Squat Knees End Position (Barbell)', 'Legs', 'Barbell', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '66241201', '66241201-Barbell-Squat---Knees---End-position-(WRONG-RIGHT)-(female)_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.133197+00', '1. Set up a barbell in a rack at the appropriate height for Barbell Squat Knees End Position. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 9, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'squat', 'Squat Knees End Position', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 5, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0e439f92-8f81-4193-b6f6-3ef02953e20a', 'Stepjack Overhead Press', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity pressing exercise that challenges your entire body. Your triceps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '57141201', '57141201-Stepjack-Overhead-Press-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'shoulder_press', 'Stepjack Overhead Press', 'lateral_raise, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e4ab405-4660-4d72-ab36-88b8fc222009', 'Standing Turn And Knee Raise', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Standing Turn And Knee Raise builds reactive power and improves conditioning. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '73511201', '73511201-Standing-Turn-and-Knee-Raise-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Standing Turn And Knee Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Standing Turn And Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e4b6aab-eacc-43be-a83e-c30ec98037de', 'Hanging Knee Raise (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Core', 'Pull-Up Bar', '{"Lower Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Hanging Knee Raise, focusing on your abs. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The hanging position challenges your grip while targeting the primary muscles. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '98191201', '98191201-Hanging-Knee-Raise-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Grip the bar and hang with arms fully extended, engaging your shoulders. 2. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Hanging Knee Raise. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_raise', 'Hanging Knee Raise', 'crunch, plank, v_up', FALSE, 'pull_up_bar', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e558273-c56c-4a34-a91a-01dd3ee48031', 'Seated Lats Focused Row (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This rowing exercise strengthens the muscles between your shoulder blades. Your biceps, rear delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '55531201', '55531201-Cable-Seated-Lats-Focused-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.466497+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Seated Lats Focused Row. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Lats Focused Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0e5c5942-233e-44c0-bd34-a3601b883b1b', 'Reverse Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Traps"}'::text[], 'Target your rear delts with the Dumbbell Reverse Fly, an effective shoulder flying exercise. You''ll also feel your upper back working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '3831201', '03831201-Dumbbell-Reverse-Fly_Shoulders-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.417605+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Reverse Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'rear_delt', 'Reverse Fly', 'bench_press, incline_bench_press, push_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0e628ada-2122-4f6b-b0a2-4a49618b4ad6', 'Standing Lateral Raise (Machine)', 'Shoulders', 'Machine', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this raising movement focusing on your lateral delts. The standing position engages your core for stability. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '88471201', '88471201-Lever-Standing-Lateral-Raise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Lateral Raise. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 4. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'lateral_raise', 'Lever Standing Lateral Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0e68c449-6b40-4e34-a29d-78e344b42e2e', 'Seated Boat Row (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '104851201', '104851201-Seated-Boat-Row-on-Chair-(male)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep tension on the target muscles throughout. This exercise is excellent for upper back development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Seated Boat Row On Chair', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e72df3c-923c-4764-81dc-cb9b955b406c', 'Assisted Weighted Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. This is a great exercise for all fitness levels with proper scaling.', '107181201', '107181201-Assisted-Weighted-Push-up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:30.54809+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout. Ideal for chest strength and endurance.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Assisted Weighted Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e8836bd-f410-4602-b5ec-95f1c8249fce', 'Calf Raise Clap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Calf Raise Clap isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '56411201', '56411201-Calf-Raise-Clap-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 2. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 3. Lower with control and repeat. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Calf Raise Clap', 'standing_calf_raise, seated_calf_raise, tibialis_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0e8e4c0c-8489-41e4-996e-523a7c3c0601', 'Learning Front Raise (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Chest"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Learning Front Raise is a raising exercise that targets your front delts for shoulder development. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '69881201', '69881201-Kettlebell-Learning-Front-Raise-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Learning Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Learning Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('0ea50b32-892e-4f71-b83c-e7117e16aa29', 'Squat Side Leg Kick (Cable)', 'Legs', 'Cables', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '104161201', '104161201-Cable-Squat-Side-Leg-Kick-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.099303+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Squat Side Leg Kick. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 95, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Squat Side Leg Kick', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0ea86656-d2a0-473f-bf51-1656d141194d', 'Seated Side Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Abs"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '54881201', '54881201-Sitting-Side-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Seated Side Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0eaa8be1-8800-409c-a4e1-1c6b84f82987', 'Star Obliques Twist High Knee', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity twisting exercise that challenges your entire body. Your hip flexors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '93521201', '93521201-Star-Obliques-Twist-High-Knee-(female)_Plyometrics.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.21093+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Star Obliques Twist High Knee. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'Star Obliques Twist High Knee', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0eb62fee-d430-4ade-8406-215ffb305aa2', 'Inner Biceps Curl - Single Arm (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'Build bigger biceps with this curling movement that targets the front of your arms. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '12031201', '12031201-Cable-One-Arm-Inner-Biceps-Curl_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable One Arm Inner Biceps Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Unilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Single Arm Inner Bicep Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0eba213d-6e33-45a1-a540-add8c4db0433', 'Standing Hip Extension (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This extension exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The standing position engages your core for stability. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '36491201', '36491201-Lever-Standing-Hip-Extension-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Hip Extension. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Extend through the target joint(s) for Lever Standing Hip Extension. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Lever Standing Hip Extension', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0ec2baa8-3e62-47a4-ad77-05a3a1ec4f16', 'Seated Neck Side Upward Stretch', 'Neck', 'Bodyweight', '{"Neck"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your neck, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The upper back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '89191201', '89191201-Seated-Neck-Side-Upward-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.288245+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Neck Side Upward Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Seated Neck Side Upward Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ed5cb9f-9a7d-4840-be9b-f47f9fa16fce', 'V Up', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '8251201', '08251201-V-up_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.79101+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for V Up. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'v_up', 'V Up', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ee3afb7-f479-47cb-9ec1-0fea5b9a24bc', 'Standing Supinated Face Pull - Towels (Towel)', 'Shoulders', 'Towel', '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back","Rotator Cuff"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise works your rear delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The upper back, rotator cuff assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '77451201', '77451201-Standing-Supinated-Face-Pull-(with-towels)_Shoulde.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.083517+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Use an underhand (supinated) grip with palms facing up/toward you. 3. Pull the rope toward your face, separating your hands as you pull. 4. Squeeze your rear delts and upper back at peak contraction. 5. Return with control, maintaining cable tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'face_pull', 'Standing Supinated Face Pull', 'rear_delt_fly, bent_over_row, lateral_raise', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ee53c89-3ca2-4ed6-a899-a90ebe1c6038', 'Tip Toe Glute Bridge', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this bridging movement that emphasizes the glutes. You''ll also feel your hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '94481201', '94481201-Tip-Toe-Glute-Bridge-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on the mind-muscle connection. An effective movement for your legs routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_bridge', 'Tip Toe Glute Bridge', 'hip_thrust, romanian_deadlift', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ef5edd3-8158-4f1e-9c07-49941fbc645c', 'Pass Through (Towel)', 'Shoulders', 'Towel', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '90111201', '90111201-Pass-Through-with-Towel-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.732034+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Pass Through With Towel. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pass_through', 'Pass Through With Towel', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f0b90dd-d9f8-409a-bc28-a3118e6fc2c2', 'Lying Floor Close Press Catch (Medicine Ball)', 'Core', 'Medicine Ball', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Medicine Ball Lying Floor Close Press Catch is a core pressing exercise that primarily targets your core. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '105981201', '105981201-Medicine-Ball-Lying-Floor-Close-Press-Catch-(male.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Hold a medicine ball at the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Lying Floor Close Press Catch. 2. Position yourself on the floor for Medicine Ball Lying Floor Close Press Catch. 3. Lie down in the appropriate position for Medicine Ball Lying Floor Close Press Catch. 4. Execute the pressing motion for Medicine Ball Lying Floor Close Press Catch, extending through the target muscles. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Medicine Ball Lying Floor Close Press Catch', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'medicine_ball', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f203330-319c-4471-a5c0-e0292a09a7ae', 'Standing Hip Hugger (Dumbbell)', 'Full Body', 'Dumbbells', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Standing Hip Hugger is an arm movement exercise targeting your full body. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '66041201', '66041201-Dumbbell-Standing-Hip-Hugger-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Standing Hip Hugger. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 64, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Standing Hip Hugger', 'hip_thrust, lunge, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0f245afd-20f0-4128-8440-e53a357aba10', 'Seated Dynamic Side Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Target your full body with this stretching stretch that helps restore range of motion. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '67231201', '67231201-Sitting-Dynamic-Side-Stretch-(front-POV)-(male)_Wa.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Move into the stretch position for Seated Dynamic Side Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Seated Dynamic Side Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f35d66d-812c-443f-8ec7-b622afd12ba2', 'Weighted Steel Mace Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '104101201', '104101201-Weighted-Steel-Mace-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.837118+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Ideal for quads strength and endurance.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Weighted Steel Mace Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f3728ab-b425-45b2-b93f-f3e1ba3d5328', 'Deadlift (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this hip hinge movement focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '3001201', '03001201-Dumbbell-Deadlift_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0f3bd3e2-3541-4536-9957-14f2808f1bf9', 'Standing Glute Back Lift (Against Wall)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this movement movement focused on hip extension. The standing position engages your core for stability. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '86581201', '86581201-Standing-Glute-Back-Lift-against-Wall-(female)_Hip.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.570929+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 44, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Standing Glute Back Lift Against Wall', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f3c2cb8-e91b-45b4-b433-e7fd4c099f11', 'Side Lying Thoracic Open Book', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Obliques"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your thoracic spine, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '82521201', '82521201-Side-Lying-Thoracic-Open-Book-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Move into the stretch position for Side Lying Thoracic Open Book. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. 5. Switch sides and repeat for equal time.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'spinal_stretch', 'Side Lying Thoracic Open Book', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f4506a6-ec3b-4ad3-9c5e-fffce3dd17c6', 'Side Plank Glute Raise (Resistance Band)', 'Core', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Abs","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Resistance Band Side Plank Glute Raise, focusing on your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '67371201', '67371201-Resistance-Band-Side-Plank-Glute-Raise-(female)_Wa.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.128549+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Side Plank Glute Raise. 2. Raise your arms out to the sides until parallel to the floor. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Glute Raise', 'shoulder_press, front_raise, rear_delt_fly, upright_row', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0f458bc0-5ac0-440f-8b24-024e90f66f82', 'Seated Upright Row (Chair)', 'Shoulders', 'Chair', '{"Side Delts"}'::text[], '{"Traps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this rowing movement focusing on your delts. Your traps work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '91201201', '91201201-Sitting-Upright-Row-on-a-Chair-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the weight straight up along your body, leading with your elbows. 4. Raise until elbows reach shoulder height, then lower with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'upright_row', 'Seated Upright Row On A Chair', 'crunch, leg_raise, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f4ca87f-4588-4fc7-9ad4-86a57c77dc4d', 'Standing Leg Calf Raise (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Calves"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Lever Standing Single Leg Calf Raise isolates your calf muscles through a raising motion. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '107231201', '107231201-Lever-Standing-Single-Leg-Calf-Raise-(female)_Cal.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.855778+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Standing Single Leg Calf Raise. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Lower your heels below the platform to get a full stretch. 4. Rise up onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves. 5. Lower with control and repeat. 6. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 7. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Lever Standing Single Leg Calf Raise', 'calf_raise, seated_calf_raise', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('0f5a4c59-4d27-4ac3-ab25-37a7d25078b3', 'Cat Cow Stretch', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your spine, the Cat Cow Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. The core assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '45801201', '45801201-Cat-Cow-Stretch_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Cat Cow Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Cat Cow Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f5c27ba-8aa9-47d9-b413-21b97500d1ea', 'Crunch Hold With Legs Off (Dumbbell)', 'Core', 'Dumbbells', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities. Keep your core engaged throughout the exercise.', '54651201', '54651201-Dumbbell-Crunch-Hold-with-Legs-Off_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Crunch Hold With Legs Off. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch Hold With Legs Off', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0f5ea064-1ffe-4630-8b95-bb2928ea96fb', 'Side Bend Arms Above', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your abs provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '66501201', '66501201-Side-Bend-Arms-Above-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.079801+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Bend Arms Above. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Side Bend Arms Above', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f5fc153-5fb9-46f3-a423-9ca47dc99933', 'Curtsey Lunge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This lunging movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '8811201', '08811201-Dumbbell-Curtsey-lunge-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Curtsey Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lunge', 'Curtsey Lunge', 'split_squat, step_up, squat', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0f709371-17e8-4eaf-b933-2e2f07f4faca', 'Control Balance', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Control Balance is a flexibility exercise that targets your full body, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '28401201', '28401201-Control-Balance_Pilates_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Control Balance. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Control Balance', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f7f9cab-b0c6-4b13-915c-e5d6d85e8f8f', 'Seated Hands Behind Chest Stretch (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your chest area and enhance overall flexibility. The shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '91741201', '91741201-Sitting-Hands-Behind-Chest-Stretch-on-a-Chair-(fem.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Move into the stretch position for Seated Hands Behind Chest Stretch On A Chair. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 25, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_stretch', 'Seated Hands Behind Chest Stretch On A Chair', 'stretch_shoulder, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f8ca0a3-7093-4f73-818c-4f1a5b65a31e', 'JM Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell JM Bench Press is an arm pressing exercise targeting your chest. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '521201', '00521201-Barbell-JM-Bench-Press_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'JM Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0f931b6e-700c-44bb-ab4b-9474ba84b61d', 'Side Crunch Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity squatting exercise that challenges your entire body. The abs assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '73391201', '73391201-Side-Crunch-Squat-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.968567+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. This variation specifically emphasizes the abs.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Side Crunch Squat', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0f93b211-5ec6-471f-8ee6-29982d442f73', 'Side Plank Clamshell (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Core","Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Abductors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this stabilization movement focusing on your glute med/abductors. Your hip abductors work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Resistance bands provide accommodating resistance that increases through the range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '98571201', '98571201-Resistance-Band-Side-Plank-Clamshell-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.890719+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Side Plank Clamshell. 2. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 3. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 4. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 75, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_plank', 'Side Plank Clamshell', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'band', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('0fac190c-718e-421a-b5c9-cc68a1016c2e', 'Inverted Legs Elevated Row - Close Grip (Step Platform)', 'Back', 'Step Platform', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Inverted Legs Elevated Close Grip Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '105041201', '105041201-Inverted-Legs-Elevated-Close-grip-Row-(male)_Back.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Inverted Legs Elevated Row - Close Grip', 'Inverted Legs Elevated Row - Close Grip', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0fac8fcc-eb9a-4b20-861a-0ccc3a6b02c4', 'Standing Chest Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing Chest Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. Your triceps, front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '10661201', '10661201-Cable-Standing-Chest-Press_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing Chest Press. 2. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Standing Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0fbb6fde-0cb6-4948-8ff4-5ca05fe8d092', 'Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench is a lower body movement exercise that targets your delts. Kneeling helps eliminate lower body momentum from the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '67401201', '67401201-Kneeling-Leg-Half-Circle-on-bench-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.487002+00', '1. Get into a half-kneeling position (one knee down, opposite foot forward). 2. Set up in the starting position for Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Kneeling Leg Half Circle On Bench', 'squat, leg_extension, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65);
INSERT INTO _exercise_staging (id, name, category, equipment, primary_muscles, secondary_muscles, description, video_code, video_filename, gender, is_custom, created_at, steps_to_perform, movement_pattern, force_type, movement_type, laterality, plane_of_motion, difficulty_level, complexity_score, strength_rating, hypertrophy_rating, power_rating, endurance_rating, body_position, bench_angle, grip_type, grip_width, optimal_rep_range_min, optimal_rep_range_max, placement_in_workout, fatigability, popularity_score, home_gym_friendly, instructions, workout_type, practicality_score, fat_loss_rating, general_fitness_rating, is_compound, supersetable, exercise_family, base_exercise_name, complementary_families, is_equipment_primary, equipment_category, duration_based, recommended_sets, rest_seconds, muscles_worked_count, priority_build_muscle, priority_get_lean, priority_home, priority_gym) VALUES
('0fc76d1b-0090-4766-866d-fbd78068f699', 'Side Lying Heel Reaches', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your core. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '69701201', '69701201-Side-Lying-Heel-Reaches-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.179953+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Set up in the starting position for Side Lying Heel Reaches. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Side Lying Heel Reaches', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0fd962b9-ae01-4fb6-bf50-3efd705f0c37', 'Step Up Bicep Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells, Step Platform', '{"Quads","Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Forearms"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this curling exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '73621201', '73621201-Dumbbell-Step-up-Biceps-Curl-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.247914+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Step Up Biceps Curl. 2. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 3. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 4. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 5. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Curl', 'Pull', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 92, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Step Up Bicep Curl', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('0fe63938-f91b-4536-9fe3-8e43b92b2835', 'Dip Bent Knees (Chair)', 'Chest', 'Chair', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this dipping exercise for bigger arms. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '71321201', '71321201-Dip-Bent-Knees-with-Chair_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.123298+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Dip Bent Knees With Chair', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0fefe0dd-6212-4c39-a856-9ecddfbe4ba5', 'Bench Press - Close Grip (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing movement isolates your triceps for improved arm development. Secondary activation of your chest provides additional muscle engagement. Barbells enable bilateral loading for building raw strength. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '301201', '00301201-Barbell-Close-Grip-Bench-Press_Upper-Arms-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Use a close/narrow grip (hands closer than shoulder-width). 3. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 4. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Bench Press (Close Grip)', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Narrow', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'close_grip_bench', 'Bench Press - Close Grip', 'Bench Press - Close Grip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('0ffac113-bf32-4bf6-8a99-1499e318ff52', 'Crunch Floor', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Crunch Floor, focusing on your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '2751201', '02751201-Crunch-Floor-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Position yourself on the floor for Crunch Floor. 2. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 3. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 4. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Crunch Floor', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('0ffbbb73-74ad-4d0b-a88f-dd00eb9a8211', 'Low Fly (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Cable Low Fly, an effective flying movement for upper body strength. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Cables provide constant tension throughout the full range of motion. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '1791201', '01791201-Cable-Low-Fly_Chest-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.263406+00', '1. Set the cable pulley to the lowest position and attach your preferred handle. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Low Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('0ffd93a9-44a3-4f99-b37d-29af0c8b6304', 'Seated Palm Pulldown (Chair)', 'Back', 'Chair', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'Build lat width and pulling strength with this pulling movement. You''ll also feel your biceps, upper back working to support the movement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '91211201', '91211201-Sitting-Palm-Pulldown-on-a-Chair-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.756436+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 4. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 5. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Seated Palm Pulldown On A Chair', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('10047fb1-06dd-4ab6-bd77-a46405e9a025', 'Side Crunch - Twisted', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Abs"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '7071201', '07071201-Side-Crunch-(version-2)_Waist-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Side Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1007e2cf-39d2-43c1-b945-975ee8893d82', 'Standing Single Leg High Knee To Butt Kick With Support', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this kicking movement focusing on your full body. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '46531201', '46531201-Standing-Single-Leg-High-Knee-to-Butt-Kick-with-Support_Hips.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Stand tall with your feet firmly planted. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 37, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_kickback', 'Standing Single Leg High Knee To Butt Kick With Support', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('100b4fc5-6503-47aa-8dea-a6734cb5edbb', 'Split Fly (TRX)', 'Shoulders', 'TRX', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this flying movement focusing on your delts. Secondary activation of your front delts provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics.', '11391201', '11391201-Suspender-Split-Fly-(female)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Split Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Suspender Split Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('100f4b5a-677f-46eb-94c4-12c813a16129', 'Counterbalanced Skater Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Counterbalanced Skater Squat is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '43631201', '43631201-Counterbalanced-Skater-Squat-(male)_Thighs.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.987963+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 85, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'balance', 'Counterbalanced Skater Squat', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1010096e-dc3e-41c9-a10a-a10e9d525ca5', 'High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension (Band)', 'Arms', 'Resistance Band, Anchor Point', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Band High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a pulling motion. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '58771201', '58771201-Band-High-Pulley-Overhead-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'High Pulley Overhead Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('101210fb-e630-43af-8c89-75d3aac23dbc', 'Incline Pigeon Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hips"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your hips, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. You''ll also feel your glutes working to support the movement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '94611201', '94611201-Incline-Pigeon-Stretch-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.667107+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Incline Pigeon Stretch. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 43, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Incline Pigeon Stretch', 'stretch_hamstring, stretch_glute, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1019792c-0ccf-42c3-84b7-bca626b9ae22', 'Step Up (Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Step Up is a stepping exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '58301201', '58301201-Bodyweight-Step-up-(VERSION-2)-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 3. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 4. Step back down with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Beneficial for overall legs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Up', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1035c1ad-b7ac-42d7-8b7a-26d89dc168b1', 'Standing Arm Crossovers And Lift', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. Your front delts work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '96151201', '96151201-Standing-Arm-Crossovers-and-Lift-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.425788+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Arm Crossovers And Lift. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Arm Crossovers And Lift', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('103b751c-d1ab-48bd-b71e-07082d7bf9ec', 'Standing Single Arm Triceps Extension (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'The Cable Standing One Arm Triceps Extension targets your triceps through a extension motion. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '26961201', '26961201-Cable-Standing-One-Arm-Triceps-Extension-(female)_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Standing One Arm Triceps Extension. 2. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 3. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 4. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 87, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Standing Single Arm Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('10621ee7-e49f-411d-8d63-72589c59e17b', 'Standing Reach Up Back Rotation Stretch', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Standing Reach Up Back Rotation Stretch is a flexibility exercise that targets your back, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '17961201', '17961201-Standing-Reach-Up-Back-Rotation-Stretch_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.341124+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Standing Reach Up Back Rotation Stretch. 3. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 42, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Standing Reach Up Back Rotation Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('10732266-5f70-4277-99d4-576c9fb5664b', 'Shrug (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Traps"}'::text[], '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], 'The Cable Shrug is a shrugging exercise that develops back strength and muscle. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '70631201', '70631201-Cable-Shrug-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.054831+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Shrug. 2. Shrug your shoulders straight up toward your ears. 3. Hold briefly at the top, then lower with control. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 80, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'shrug', 'Shrug', 'deadlift, bent_over_row, face_pull', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('10835ecb-801d-40f9-86c8-24712448fead', 'Seated Back Squeeze', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger back with this movement movement targeting your core. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '51281201', '51281201-Seated-Back-Squeeze-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.581585+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Seated Back Squeeze. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your core. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Seated Back Squeeze', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1087b9ba-ba6c-4774-879c-b940e04ec09e', 'Weighted Seated Plate Driver', 'Shoulders', 'Bodyweight', '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], '{"Traps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise works your delts for improved shoulder strength and aesthetics. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '65851201', '65851201-Weighted-Seated-Plate-Driver-(male)_Shoulders_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Seated Plate Driver. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your delts. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Weighted Seated Plate Driver', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1094115d-84e3-42cc-97ec-9deb87910a36', 'Jump Split', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'This dynamic jumping movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. The quads, calves assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '11661201', '11661201-Jump-Split-(male)_Plyometrics-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Jump Split. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat_jump', 'Jump Split', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('109c3f00-b62d-485e-ae7e-e667c73015a8', 'Side Stretch Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'This crunching exercise engages your abs for improved core stability and strength. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '7191201', '07191201-Side-Stretch-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Perfect for targeting your abs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 60, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'lat_stretch', 'Side Stretch Crunch', 'plank, leg_raise, russian_twist, sit_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('109c77ff-3470-47a8-ae7e-eb69f35e1bf4', 'Glute Ham Raise', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Glute Ham Raise is a hip-dominant raising exercise that targets your glutes. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '44561201', '44561201-Glute-Ham-Raise-(VERSION-2)_Thighs-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.145158+00', '1. Raise the weight in the prescribed direction for Glute Ham Raise. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Glute Ham Raise', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('109fae3b-65bb-423d-aba1-e1bd94eb60da', 'Glute Press (Machine)', 'Legs', 'Machine', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this pressing movement focused on hip extension. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '66011201', '66011201-Lever-Glute-Press-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Glute Press. 2. Execute the pressing motion for Lever Glute Press, extending through the target muscles. 3. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'glute_exercise', 'Lever Glute Press', 'hip_thrust, glute_bridge, leg_curl', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('10b33b03-8a7d-4856-804c-02de9f604ba8', 'Weighted Svend Press', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pressing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '8561201', '08561201-Weighted-Svend-Press_Chest-FIX_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.233728+00', '1. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 2. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squeeze_press', 'Weighted Svend Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('10b4ba21-5c6f-4389-ba23-98135f80f79a', 'Weighted Hollow Body Hover', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '76881201', '76881201-Weighted-Hollow-Body-Hover-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.483269+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Weighted Hollow Body Hover. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hollow_hold', 'Weighted Hollow Body Hover', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('10c20efb-a25f-470b-9a95-e3005cf140b1', 'Standing Two Side Bend (Bent Arm)', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your abs. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '32561201', '32561201-Standing-Two-Side-Bend-(bent-arm)-(female)_Waist.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Two Side Bend. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'side_bend', 'Standing Two Side Bend', 'russian_twist, woodchop, oblique_crunch', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('10e47b56-6ed6-4502-a8f5-6be9e7e4e791', 'Side Step Deep Squat', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this squatting exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '71681201', '71681201-Side-Step-Deep-Squat-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.303932+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. This variation specifically emphasizes the quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Side Step Deep Squat', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('10f66957-8fa6-46ee-b79f-75a0974e23d8', 'Bridge Pose Setu Bandhasana', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your full body, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The glutes, chest, shoulders assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '45111201', '45111201-Bridge-Pose-Setu-Bandhasana-(male)_Stretching.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Bridge Pose Setu Bandhasana. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Bridge Pose Setu Bandhasana', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, plank', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('1116382f-534e-46b7-a3ad-0fa904126594', 'Slight Squat Hand Swipe', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Slight Squat Hand Swipe is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic squatting movements. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '93461201', '93461201-Slight-Squat-Hand-Swipe-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.99429+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. Great for building strength in your quads. Variation: Slight Squat Hand Swipe.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Slight Squat Hand Swipe', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1123552b-3a85-44d3-89bc-63ea01c07c03', 'Mountain Climber Push Up (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this pushing movement that works your abs. Secondary activation of your hip flexors, shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. The TRX allows you to adjust difficulty by changing your body angle. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '11211201', '11211201-Suspender-Mountain-Climber-Push-up-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Mountain Climber Push Up. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 60, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Suspender Mountain Climber Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip, tricep_pushdown', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('1134699d-6002-4cc8-abd0-20c4318caf16', 'Seated Tip Toe Clap (Chair)', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This movement movement focuses on your gastrocnemius and soleus. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '90861201', '90861201-Sitting-Tip-Toe-Clap-on-a-Chair-(female)_Plyometri.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.877283+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement. This variation specifically emphasizes the calves.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Seated Tip Toe Clap On A Chair', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1136161d-51a2-409d-b7c1-96ba3c0901e7', 'Toe Jump', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this jumping exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Your quads, calves work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '49041201', '49041201-Toe-Jump-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.623429+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Toe Jump. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'tuck_jump', 'Toe Jump', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('113ee621-1d51-4fbc-b318-6c20a2a54e64', 'Squat To Leg Extension And Torso Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Squat To Leg Extension And Torso Twist is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '80691201', '80691201-Squat-to-Leg-Extension-and-Torso-Twist-(female)_Th.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.285955+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Don''t rush—quality over quantity. Include this in your legs training.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 100, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'leg_extension', 'Squat To Leg Extension And Torso Twist', 'squat, leg_press, lunge', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11402022-0e28-4ed4-b547-d74f5dc1efa9', 'JM Tricep Press (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Machine', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this pressing exercise for bigger arms. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Machine exercises are great for isolating muscles and training to failure safely. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '98601201', '98601201-Lever-Sitting-JM-Press-(male)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.689343+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Seated JM Press. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Execute the pressing motion for Lever Seated JM Press, extending through the target muscles. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lever Seated JM Press', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('114051d5-17c0-4837-a122-1c30e4466116', 'Romanian Deadlift To Squat (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads","Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'This squatting movement emphasizes your quadriceps for stronger, more powerful legs. Secondary activation of your glutes, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '94841201', '94841201-Dumbbell-Romanian-Deadlift-to-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.577164+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Romanian Deadlift To Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, 6, NULL, 10, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Romanian Deadlift To Squat', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 6, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('11451581-a249-4bff-be6d-6dfaee7fede6', 'Preacher Curl - Rope (Cable)', 'Arms', 'Cables', '{"Biceps"}'::text[], '{"Forearms"}'::text[], 'The Cable Preacher Curl (rope Attachment) is a curling exercise that isolates your biceps. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '59231201', '59231201-Cable-Preacher-Curl-(rope-attachment)_Upper-Arms_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Preacher Curl. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'preacher_curl', 'Preacher Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, bicep_curl, hammer_curl', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('1152e3a3-e24b-48ab-a76e-19e697c265b1', 'Standing Fly', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. The front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The standing position engages your core for stability. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '48731201', '48731201-Bodyweight-Standing-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Stand with feet about shoulder-width apart. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 72, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Standing Fly', 'bench_press, incline_press, push_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11578fce-d19d-435d-836c-d48c62d41b5f', 'Riding Outdoor Bicycle', 'Core', 'Door Frame', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Riding Outdoor Bicycle is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. You''ll also feel your abs working to support the movement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '52151201', '52151201-Riding-Outdoor-Bicycle-(female)_Cardio_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Riding Outdoor Bicycle. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cycling', 'Riding Outdoor Bicycle', 'running, elliptical, rowing_cardio', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1159062e-2a1f-4fd6-bb35-2af4f8723893', 'Squat And Tip Toes', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Squat And Tip Toes is a squatting exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '77411201', '77411201-Squat-and-Tip-Toes-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:20.982555+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'calf_raise', 'Squat And Tip Toes', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
