('117cc378-d5af-4c9b-93ea-e19d0f5259d3', 'Hyght Fly (Dumbbell)', 'Chest', 'Dumbbells, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this flying movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your front delts working to support the movement. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '34241201', '34241201-Hyght-Dumbbell-Fly-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Hyght Dumbbell Fly. 2. With a slight bend in your elbows, move the weight in a wide arc. 3. Squeeze your chest muscles at the center/top of the movement. 4. Return with control, feeling the stretch at the bottom. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'chest_fly', 'Hyght Fly', 'Hyght Fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('1182df8d-43c1-4ba0-819a-9b5fc967be08', 'Deep Squat Turn', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'This stretch specifically works on your quads, promoting flexibility and reducing muscle tightness. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '79081201', '79081201-Deep-Squat-Turn-(female)_Stretching_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control. Beneficial for overall stretching development.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Deep Squat Turn', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1182e37a-54f1-43e6-9479-86d964403c3e', 'Prone Incline Flexion Row (Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Incline Bench', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'The Dumbbell Prone Incline Flexion Row is a rowing exercise that builds thickness in your upper back. Secondary activation of your biceps, rear delts provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '106411201', '106411201-Dumbbell-Prone-Incline-Flexion-Row_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.242428+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Prone Incline Flexion Row. 2. Lie face down (prone position) for Dumbbell Prone Incline Flexion Row. 3. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 4. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 5. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'general_exercise', 'Prone Incline Flexion Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('11875c9c-cae1-48f6-ad4d-54bfbbb2c2fd', 'Leg Kickback (Resistance Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'This kicking exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Bands are joint-friendly and portable, perfect for any training environment. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '72811201', '72811201-Resistance-Band-Leg-Kickback-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.831811+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Resistance Band Leg Kickback. 2. Keep your upper arm stationary and extend your forearm back. 3. Squeeze at full extension, then return with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Control the movement—avoid using momentum.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_kickback', 'Leg Kickback', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('1187a95c-1557-4c12-9cb6-017179de4eca', 'Lying Sole To Sole Groin Stretch', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Lying Sole To Sole Groin Stretch provides a deep stretch for your adductors, ideal for recovery and mobility work. Secondary activation of your hips provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '85661201', '85661201-Lying-Sole-To-Sole-Groin-Stretch-(female)_Stretchi.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Sole To Sole Groin Stretch. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Sole To Sole Groin Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Lying Sole To Sole Groin Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1189f810-207e-4697-a40e-808c40a94f01', 'Wide Legged Forward Bend Prasarita Padottanasana', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your hamstrings with this movement stretch that helps restore range of motion. You''ll also feel your lower back, calves working to support the movement. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '9651201', '09651201-Wide-legged-Forward-Bend-Prasarita-Padottanasana-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Move into the stretch position for Wide Legged Forward Bend Prasarita Padottanasana (. 2. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 3. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 15, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'yoga', 'Wide Legged Forward Bend Prasarita Padottanasana (', 'squat, lunge, leg_press', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('119be452-bd45-4cdf-817c-636444645a71', 'Advanced Windmill (Kettlebell)', 'Core', 'Kettlebell', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Advanced Windmill is a core movement exercise that primarily targets your abs. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Building core stability helps with everything from heavy deadlifts to daily activities.', '5171201', '05171201-Kettlebell-Advanced-Windmill_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Advanced Windmill. 2. Set up in the starting position for Kettlebell Advanced Windmill. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your abs. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'windmill', 'Advanced Windmill', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('11a054f8-bf9b-4152-bab3-43635935c741', 'Standing Good Morning', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Glutes"}'::text[], 'This movement movement works your hamstrings for balanced leg development. The glutes, lower back assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '98611201', '98611201-Bodyweight-Standing-Good-Morning-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Bodyweight Standing Good Morning. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Standing Good Morning', 'romanian_deadlift, back_extension, hip_thrust', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11a7a5d0-6a6b-4825-9cf9-d76df08f9265', 'High Lunge To Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Use this stretch to open up your hamstrings area and enhance overall flexibility. Your lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Include this in your routine for better mobility and reduced muscle tension.', '79011201', '79011201-High-Lunge-to-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_Stretchin.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for High Lunge To Hamstring Stretch. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 48, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'High Lunge To Hamstring Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('11a808f3-a564-43cf-9f57-44932f4b7f5b', 'Seated Wide Side Adduction - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Inner Thighs"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this movement movement focusing on your adductors. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Focus on controlled form throughout each repetition.', '67111201', '67111201-Seated-Alternate-Wide-Side-Adduction-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.644637+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_adduction', 'Seated Wide Side Adduction - Alternating', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11ac7041-fffb-4bc2-b4d0-35cf2c8f56e2', 'Standing Wide Stance Punch', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Standing Wide Stance Punch, an effective movement movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this standing challenges your balance and core engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '88331201', '88331201-Standing-Wide-Stance-Punch-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.992671+00', '1. Begin in a standing position with good posture. 2. Set up in the starting position for Standing Wide Stance Punch. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your chest. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Standing', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'boxing', 'Standing Wide Stance Punch', 'core_exercise, shoulder_exercise, burpee', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11b8bdd2-4e0d-4472-a399-d71949a34d45', 'Over Bench Single Arm Neutral Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this curling exercise. The forearms assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements.', '3661201', '03661201-Dumbbell-Over-Bench-One-Arm-Neutral-Wrist-Curl_For.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.146796+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Over Bench Single Arm Neutral Wrist Curl', 'tricep_pushdown, tricep_extension, hammer_curl, preacher_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('11d4994b-68ae-405d-b0b0-8cf69f2afa69', 'Hip Thrust (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'This thrusting exercise isolates your glutes for improved hip strength and power. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '57541201', '57541201-Dumbbell-Hip-Thrust-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Hip Thrust. 2. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 3. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 4. Lower your hips back down with control. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('11d773e2-54ee-4394-88ae-e6d3fd7a006d', 'Incline Reverse Hyperextension (Hyperextension Bench)', 'Back', 'Hyperextension Bench', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Develop your posterior chain with this extension movement that emphasizes the glutes. Secondary activation of your hamstrings, lower back provides additional muscle engagement. The incline angle shifts emphasis toward the upper portion of the target muscles. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '68761201', '68761201-Incline-Reverse-Hyperextension-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.678791+00', '1. Raise your torso by extending at the lower back/hips. 2. Lower with control, maintaining tension. 3. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 73, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_extension', 'Incline Reverse Hyperextension', 'good_morning, bird_dog, superman', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11d79cf7-e7f2-4e30-8357-b9ab58f6bf75', 'Side Lying Single Leg Kick', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Side Lying Single Leg Kick is a kicking exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '89471201', '89471201-Side-Lying-Single-Leg-Kick-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 45, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'leg_exercise', 'Side Lying Single Leg Kick', 'hip_flexor, lunge, dynamic_warmup', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11dab33e-2c67-47fc-8c6e-c42584518d0a', 'Lying Legs Curl - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hamstrings"}'::text[], '{"Glutes"}'::text[], 'Build leg strength with this curling movement focusing on your biceps. Secondary activation of your forearms provides additional muscle engagement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Leg training boosts metabolism and builds functional, real-world strength.', '71291201', '71291201-Bodyweight-Lying-Alternate-Legs-Curl-(female)_Thig.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.475486+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Bodyweight Lying Alternate Legs Curl. 2. Curl your heels toward your glutes by bending at the knees. 3. Squeeze your hamstrings at peak contraction. 4. Extend legs back out with control. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'bicep_curl', 'Lying Legs Curl - Alternating', 'hammer_curl, preacher_curl, cable_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11f16754-87b0-422b-b79f-a03e75633aeb', 'Bar Lateral Pulldown (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function.', '22471201', '22471201-Cable-Bar-Lateral-Pulldown-(female)_Back-FIX_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.723232+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Bar Lateral Pulldown. 2. Pull the bar/handle down toward your upper chest. 3. Drive your elbows down and back, squeezing your lats. 4. Control the weight back up without letting it yank your arms. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep the movement smooth and controlled.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'lat_pulldown', 'Bar Lateral Pulldown', 'pull_up, bent_over_row, cable_row, face_pull', TRUE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('11f3f991-3542-40f6-bc9d-b7b66274c1dc', 'Single Arm Push Up (Wall Supported)', 'Chest', 'Wall', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Single Arm Push Up Supported Wall is a pushing exercise that targets your chest muscles. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '46171201', '46171201-Single-Arm-Push-Up-Supported-Wall_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.056255+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 3. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 4. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Single Arm Push Up Supported Wall', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('11fece1b-11df-48e8-abd1-117e15f05654', 'Inchworm And Mountain Climbers', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Elevate your training with this climbing exercise that develops speed, power, and coordination. Secondary activation of your hip flexors, shoulders provides additional muscle engagement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '88161201', '88161201-Inchworm-and-Mountain-Climbers-(female)_Plyometric.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.073704+00', '1. From plank position, drive one knee toward your chest. 2. Quickly switch legs, bringing the other knee forward. 3. Continue alternating at a quick pace while maintaining plank form. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'mountain_climber', 'Inchworm And Mountain Climbers', 'burpee, plank, high_knees', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('120432c0-e882-46f2-9138-9693f7140fec', 'Elevated Split Squat (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this squatting movement that develops leg drive and power. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '93151201', '93151201-Elevated-Split-Squat-(male)_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.808474+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. An effective movement for your legs routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Elevated Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('120775fd-e33b-4cb6-968e-73b5b8bd06d6', 'High Knee Run', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], '{"Quads","Calves"}'::text[], 'The High Knee Run is a cardiovascular exercise that improves endurance and heart health. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Cardiovascular exercise improves heart health, endurance, and helps manage weight.', '38171201', '38171201-High-Knee-Run-(female)_Cardio.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.960339+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for High Knee Run. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your cardio. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'high_knees', 'High Knee Run', 'butt_kicks, jumping_jack, mountain_climber', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1212899e-2d69-4a69-809f-10c7a2073e5a', 'Bear Crawl (low Hip)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'This dynamic movement movement gets your heart rate up while developing explosive strength. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning. Excellent for pre-exhausting the target muscle before compound lifts.', '65991201', '65991201-Bear-Crawl-(low-hip)-(male)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.249384+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Bear Crawl. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Cardio', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bear_crawl', 'Bear Crawl', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('121947b9-a92a-4656-a20f-cbb226c1df41', 'Wrist Extensor Stretch', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this stretching exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '18491201', '18491201-Wrist-Extensor-Stretch-(female)_Forearms_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.146812+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Wrist Extensor Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Wrist Extensor Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('12203f66-7b1c-4d95-b8c3-72272fbef20d', 'Goblet Lunge (Dumbbell)', 'Legs', 'Dumbbells', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build stronger quads with this lunging movement that develops leg drive and power. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '78681201', '78681201-Dumbbell-Goblet-Lunge_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:25.87243+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Goblet Lunge. 2. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 3. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'goblet_squat', 'Goblet Lunge', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('1233fef4-e6bc-4b3d-ba21-5a9e92f574f5', 'Gate Openers (advanced)', 'Full Body', 'Bodyweight', '{"Full Body"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'The Gate Openers (advanced) is an explosive exercise that combines cardiovascular training with dynamic movement movements. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Plyometric training builds explosive power that transfers to sports and daily activities.', '80661201', '80661201-Gate-Openers-(advanced)-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.778367+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Gate Openers. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your full body. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 50, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'general_exercise', 'Gate Openers', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1237899c-ade2-47d5-bd47-b877ce60148d', 'Front Raise - Single (Dumbbell)', 'Shoulders', 'Dumbbells', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Abs"}'::text[], 'Target your front delts with the Dumbbell Front Raise, an effective shoulder raising exercise. Using dumbbells requires more stabilization than barbell variations. Shoulder development enhances both performance and upper body aesthetics. Aim for full range of motion on every rep.', '34281201', '34281201-Dumbbell-Front-Raise-(VERSION-2)-(female)_Shoulder.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.735372+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Front Raise. 2. Raise the weight in front of you to shoulder height. 3. Lower with control, maintaining tension throughout. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability. Include this in your shoulders training.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 82, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'front_raise', 'Front Raise', 'shoulder_press, lateral_raise, rear_delt_fly', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('1247a712-a9ff-4cde-a97b-726254103c1a', 'Twisting Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Work your side abdominals with this crunching exercise that strengthens your obliques. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '46201201', '46201201-Twisting-Crunch_Waist.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 2. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 3. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Maintain a neutral spine throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 62, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Twisting Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1248a619-6dc4-4240-94f3-ddd151119e94', 'Seesaw Press (Kettlebell)', 'Shoulders', 'Kettlebell', '{"Front Delts"}'::text[], '{"Side Delts","Triceps"}'::text[], 'Build stronger shoulders with this pressing movement focusing on your delts. Kettlebells are excellent for building functional, real-world strength. Strong shoulders improve overhead strength and support nearly all upper body movements.', '5471201', '05471201-Kettlebell-Seesaw-Press_Shoulders.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:26.39056+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Seesaw Press. 2. Start with the weight at shoulder level. 3. Press directly overhead until your arms are fully extended. 4. Lower back to shoulder level with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squeeze_press', 'Seesaw Press', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('12567668-df3a-4e5a-9659-c1a9761f4b4c', 'Seated Palm Push And March (Chair) - Alternating', 'Legs', 'Chair', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Build power and athleticism with this high-intensity pushing exercise that challenges your entire body. Secondary activation of your hip flexors provides additional muscle engagement. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. Great for improving athletic performance, burning calories, and building conditioning.', '90821201', '90821201-Sitting-Alternate-Palm-Push-and-March-on-a-Chair-(.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:37.628647+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Alternate between sides/arms/legs with each repetition. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Start with lighter weight to perfect your form.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 35, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'marching', 'Seated Palm Push And March On A Chair ( - Alternating', 'high_knees, butt_kicks, jumping_jack', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('125ccdd6-8b4f-4510-8dc4-a094adf8d0bb', 'Single Arm Reverse Wrist Curl (Dumbbell)', 'Arms', 'Dumbbells', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this curling exercise. Your forearms work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Dumbbells allow each arm to work independently, helping correct imbalances. Arm strength supports grip, pulling, and pushing in compound movements. Control the negative portion for maximum muscle engagement.', '69961201', '69961201-Dumbbell-One-Arm-Reverse-Wrist-Curl-(female)_Forea.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:33.034396+00', '1. Select an appropriate weight dumbbell and hold it in one hand. 2. Keep your elbows in a fixed position throughout the movement. 3. Curl the weight up by contracting your biceps, squeezing at the top. 4. Lower with control, resisting the weight on the way down. 5. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 6. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain consistent tempo throughout the set.', 'Curl', 'Pull', NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'wrist_curl', 'Single Arm Reverse Wrist Curl', 'hammer_curl, wrist_curl, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('1268a2f4-f853-4002-a482-36b01da2be61', 'Plank Hand Switch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Shoulders","Lower Back"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this stabilization movement that works your abs. Your shoulders, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '69601201', '69601201-Plank-Hand-Switch-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.941834+00', '1. Hold your body in a straight line from head to heels. 2. Don''t let your hips sag or pike up—engage your core and glutes. 3. Breathe steadily while maintaining the position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your shoulders relaxed and away from your ears. This exercise is excellent for abs development.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'plank', 'Plank Hand Switch', 'side_plank, dead_bug, hollow_hold', TRUE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('12792206-a8cc-4257-bdd8-fdef11d163d5', 'Squat To Straddle', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target your quads with this squatting stretch that helps restore range of motion. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '85471201', '85471201-Squat-to-Straddle-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Don''t rush—quality over quantity.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'groin_stretch', 'Squat To Straddle', 'leg_press, leg_extension, leg_curl, lunge, front_squat, hack_squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1286ff21-1a71-452a-9615-7a2da2b4ad5c', 'Renegade Row (Stability Ball, Dumbbell)', 'Back', 'Dumbbells, Stability Ball', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this rowing movement that works your upper back. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The dumbbell variation provides freedom of movement and greater range of motion. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '82231201', '82231201-Dumbbell-Renegade-Row-on-Stability-Ball-(male)_Wai.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:23.586683+00', '1. Select a pair of dumbbells at an appropriate weight for Dumbbell Renegade Row On Stability Ball. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 74, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'dumbbell_row', 'Renegade Row On Stability Ball', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', TRUE, 'dumbbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 92, 90, 92, 90),
('12c57638-22a1-43fd-a0c9-debd47eea114', 'Seated Chest Out Hands Behind (hold) On A Padded S', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this movement movement that works your core. Being seated provides stability, allowing you to focus on the working muscles. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts.', '80401201', '80401201-Seated-Chest-Out-Hands-Behind-(Hold)-on-a-padded-s.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.717157+00', '1. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 2. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Focus on the mind-muscle connection.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 52, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'chest_exercise', 'Seated Chest Out Hands Behind  On A Padded S', 'Seated Chest Out Hands Behind On A Padded S', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('12cfeec8-e404-4fe8-b05d-ded083405562', 'Side Wrist Pull Stretch', 'Arms', 'Bodyweight', '{"Forearms"}'::text[], '{}'::text[], 'Build grip strength and forearm size with this pulling exercise. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '7211201', '07211201-Side-Wrist-Pull-Stretch_Forearms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.422129+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Side Wrist Pull Stretch. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your forearms. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Ensure full range of motion on each rep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'stretch_general', 'Side Wrist Pull Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_back, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('12d26e67-38af-45fa-a998-3477f8cb7bdb', 'Deep Push Up Hold', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger chest with this pushing movement that develops pressing power. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '79851201', '79851201-Deep-Push-Up-Hold-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.501166+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Hold the position for the prescribed time, maintaining tension. Engage your stabilizer muscles for better control.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Deep Push Up Hold', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('12d56376-bcb3-4732-9222-735b592e12b8', 'Single Arm Bench Press (Cable)', 'Chest', 'Cables', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Cable Single Arm Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The cable setup allows you to adjust the angle of resistance. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '79321201', '79321201-Cable-Single-Arm-Bench-Press_Chest_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.995567+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Single Arm Bench Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Single Arm Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('12eb5155-ada9-4cc8-9930-afac286bcef3', 'Tricep Extension (Machine)', 'Arms', 'Machine', '{"Triceps"}'::text[], '{"Chest","Shoulders"}'::text[], 'Build stronger triceps with this extension exercise for bigger arms. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Dedicated arm training builds both strength and muscular definition.', '10331201', '10331201-Lever-Triceps-Extension_Upper-Arms.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.452942+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Triceps Extension. 2. Extend at the elbow until your arm is straight, squeezing the tricep. 3. Lower with control, keeping your upper arm stationary. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 10, 15, NULL, 4, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 88, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'tricep_extension', 'Lever Triceps Extension', 'tricep_pushdown, close_grip_bench', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('12ebdef1-0a68-4a3c-973f-02be17e2528c', 'T-Bar Row - Reverse Grip (Machine)', 'Back', 'Machine', '{"Obliques"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors","Abs"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. Secondary activation of your biceps, lats provides additional muscle engagement. The fixed path allows you to focus purely on muscular effort. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '31041201', '31041201-Lever-Reverse-T-Bar-Row-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:34.724336+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Reverse T Bar Row. 2. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 3. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 4. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 't_bar_row', 'Lever Reverse T Bar Row', 'bent_over_row, lat_pulldown, deadlift', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('12f42c45-0ead-4d61-b6a5-32121f5336ee', 'Lying Side Reverse Crunch', 'Core', 'Bodyweight', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Build a stronger core with the Lying Side Reverse Crunch, focusing on your abs. You''ll also feel your hip flexors working to support the movement. Performing this lying down removes momentum for stricter form. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Core strength is foundational for athletic performance and injury prevention.', '52591201', '52591201-Lying-Side-Reverse-Crunch-(female)_Waist_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.38119+00', '1. Lie on your side with your body aligned. 2. Lift your hips off the floor by contracting your lower abs. 3. Bring your knees toward your chest, then lower with control. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Focus on squeezing the target muscle at peak contraction.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'crunch', 'Lying Side Reverse Crunch', 'leg_raise, plank, russian_twist, v_up', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1302f7d4-bf5b-496b-85df-a62b200c7abf', 'Seated Straight Leg Crunch (Chair)', 'Core', 'Chair', '{"Abs"}'::text[], '{"Hip Flexors"}'::text[], 'Strengthen your midsection with this crunching movement that works your abs. The hip flexors assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The seated position helps isolate the target muscles by removing momentum. A strong core improves posture, protects your spine, and enhances all other lifts. Start with lighter weight to master the movement pattern.', '104921201', '104921201-Seated-Straight-Leg-Crunch-on-Chair-(male)_Waist_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.61214+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Sit with your back supported, core engaged, feet flat on the floor. 3. Curl your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs. 4. Don''t pull on your neck—focus on the abdominal contraction. 5. Lower with control, maintaining some tension. 6. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Exhale during the exertion phase of the movement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 5, 7, NULL, 6, 'Seated', NULL, NULL, NULL, 12, 20, NULL, 4, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 57, 5, 7, FALSE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Seated Straight Leg Crunch On Chair', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('130c75ee-df84-47a5-8bc1-0f8f1c87ce3c', 'Deadlift (Kettlebell)', 'Back', 'Kettlebell', '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings","Traps"}'::text[], 'The Kettlebell Deadlift is a lower body hip hinge exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. You''ll also feel your glutes, lower back working to support the movement. The kettlebell grip position adds a unique training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '33221201', '33221201-Kettlebell-deadlift_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:22.536005+00', '1. Select an appropriately weighted kettlebell for Kettlebell Deadlift. 2. Hinge at hips and bend knees to grip the weight. 3. Drive through your heels, extending hips and knees to stand. 4. Lower by reversing the movement with control. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 93, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'deadlift', 'Deadlift', 'romanian_deadlift, hip_thrust, leg_curl', FALSE, 'kettlebell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 75, 88, 88, 78),
('132230c9-6358-4df4-85cd-0e1d25d449f5', 'Pull Up With Bent Knee (Pull-Up Bar)', 'Back', 'Pull-Up Bar, Chair', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Biceps","Upper Back"}'::text[], 'This pulling exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Secondary activation of your biceps, upper back provides additional muscle engagement. Back development is crucial for pulling strength and overall upper body function. Perfect for including in both strength and hypertrophy programs.', '71031201', '71031201-Pull-up-with-Bent-Knee-between-Chairs-(female)_Bac.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.801913+00', '1. Position yourself with a sturdy chair for support or as part of the movement. 2. Pull yourself up by driving your elbows down and back. 3. Continue until your chin clears the bar, then lower with control to a full hang. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 55, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'pull_up', 'Pull Up With Bent Knee Between Chairs', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, bicep_curl', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1322b87d-d105-4026-a2f5-38a209806b1a', 'Wide Squat (Wall Supported)', 'Legs', 'Wall', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. You''ll also feel your glutes, hamstrings working to support the movement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '99081201', '99081201-Wide-Squat-Wall-Supported-(female)_Hips_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:40.037451+00', '1. Position yourself at the appropriate distance from a wall. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Control the movement—avoid using momentum. Great for building strength in your quads.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 77, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Wide Squat Wall Supported', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('13296e0a-2fbf-4ba2-8e80-972efbba9c98', 'Ring High Row (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Back', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Upper Back"}'::text[], '{"Lats","Biceps","Rear Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your rhomboids and mid-traps with this rowing movement. The biceps, rear delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '52691201', '52691201-Ring-High-Row-(female)_Back_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.38616+00', '1. Pull the weight toward your torso, leading with your elbow(s). 2. Squeeze your shoulder blades together at the peak contraction. 3. Extend back out with control, feeling the stretch in your back. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability. A solid choice for back day.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 58, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'cable_row', 'Ring High Row', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('132d711b-fff1-4d11-8d85-ed9f2c822802', 'Self Assisted Chest Dip (TRX)', 'Chest', 'TRX', '{"Lower Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Suspender Self Assisted Chest Dip, an effective dipping movement for upper body strength. Secondary activation of your triceps, front delts provides additional muscle engagement. Suspension training adds instability, increasing core activation throughout. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '10931201', '10931201-Suspender-Self-Assisted-Chest-Dip-(female)_Chest.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:39.472701+00', '1. Adjust the TRX/suspension straps to the appropriate length for Suspender Self Assisted Chest Dip. 2. Lower your body by bending your elbows to about 90 degrees. 3. Push back up until your arms are fully extended. 4. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 60, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'dip', 'Suspender Self Assisted Chest Dip', 'bench_press, tricep_pushdown, push_up', TRUE, 'trx', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 68, 85, 85, 70),
('1359fe38-e25c-46d0-ac7c-4b23d929edcb', 'Bench Press (Barbell)', 'Chest', 'Barbell, Flat Bench', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Barbell Bench Press is a pressing exercise that targets your chest muscles. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. The barbell allows you to handle heavier loads for maximum strength gains. A well-developed chest contributes to upper body strength and aesthetics.', '251201', '00251201-Barbell-Bench-Press_Chest-FIX2_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.67144+00', '1. Load a barbell and set it on a bench rack at the appropriate height. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep your core engaged for stability.', 'Horizontal Press', 'Push', 'Compound', 'Bilateral', NULL, 3, NULL, 10, 10, NULL, 4, 'Lying', NULL, 'Overhand (Pronated)', 'Standard', 5, 8, NULL, 8, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 97, 7, 9, TRUE, FALSE, 'bench_press', 'Bench Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 4, 120, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('135b7015-224c-4e63-9b73-e8d9873462d7', 'Split Stance RDL (Trap Bar)', 'Legs', 'Trap Bar', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Trap Bar Split Stance RDL is a lower body movement exercise that targets your hamstrings/glutes. Your glutes, lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '36521201', '36521201-Trap-Bar-Split-Stance-RDL_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.260518+00', '1. Set up in the starting position for Trap Bar Split Stance RDL. 2. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your hamstrings/glutes. 3. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'romanian_deadlift', 'Split Stance RDL', 'deadlift, leg_curl, hip_thrust', TRUE, 'barbell', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 95, 80, 65, 95),
('13666911-1958-43ad-bd7d-722413b01a2d', 'Clock Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'This pushing exercise focuses on your pectorals for improved chest strength and development. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts. Progress gradually by increasing resistance over time.', '90081201', '90081201-Clock-Push-Up-(female)_Chest_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:32.374165+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Clock Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('136c4904-20fd-4b85-a955-ca6c5447c926', 'Split Squat (Band)', 'Legs', 'Resistance Band', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Target the front of your thighs with this squatting exercise for quad development. Your glutes, hamstrings work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. The band creates increasing tension as it stretches, challenging the lockout. Strong legs are the foundation for athletic performance and functional fitness.', '41351201', '41351201-Band-Split-Squat_Thighs_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:24.307972+00', '1. Secure the resistance band appropriately for Band Split Squat. 2. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 3. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 4. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. 5. Continue for your target rep count, maintaining good form throughout.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 90, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'split_squat', 'Split Squat', 'lunge, bulgarian_split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'band', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 60, 85, 90, 50),
('1375b9b1-eff0-4e49-a025-87526ffa4e24', 'Lying Lower Back Stretch (Bent Knee)', 'Back', 'Bodyweight', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Lower Back"}'::text[], 'The Lying Lower Back Stretch (bent Knee) is a flexibility exercise that targets your back, helping to release tension and improve range of motion. The lying position provides back support and helps isolate the target muscles. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '32421201', '32421201-Lying-Lower-Back-Stretch-(bent-knee)-(female)_Back.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.250398+00', '1. Lie down in the appropriate position for Lying Lower Back Stretch. 2. Move into the stretch position for Lying Lower Back Stretch. 3. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 4. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, 'Lying', NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 40, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'back_stretch', 'Lying Lower Back Stretch', 'stretch_hip, stretch_hamstring, stretch_shoulder', FALSE, 'bodyweight', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('13798d59-a425-429a-8958-3dac8bbb3b00', 'Lat Prayers - Rope (Cable)', 'Back', 'Cables', '{"Lats"}'::text[], '{"Triceps"}'::text[], 'This movement exercise emphasizes your lats for improved back development. Cable resistance creates smooth, continuous muscle engagement. A strong back improves posture, prevents injury, and balances pressing movements.', '106421201', '106421201-Cable-Lat-Prayers-(rope-attachment)_Back_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:27.937212+00', '1. Adjust the cable machine to the correct height and attachment for Cable Lat Prayers. 2. Set up in the starting position for Cable Lat Prayers. 3. Execute the movement with proper form, focusing on your lats. 4. Control both the lifting and lowering phases of the movement. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 8, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 37, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'back_exercise', 'Lat Prayers', 'lat_pulldown, bent_over_row, pull_up', FALSE, 'cable', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 85, 88, 30, 92),
('137e6398-4dd6-4b51-9eb5-fe0e74e1f4d0', 'Elevated Single Leg Hip Thrust (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Glutes"}'::text[], '{"Hamstrings","Core"}'::text[], 'Build stronger glutes with this thrusting movement focused on hip extension. Secondary activation of your hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. No equipment needed—your body provides all the resistance. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '73721201', '73721201-Elevated-Single-Leg-Hip-Thrust-(male)_Hips_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:21.608253+00', '1. Drive through your heels to lift your hips toward the ceiling. 2. Squeeze your glutes hard at the top of the movement. 3. Lower your hips back down with control. 4. Complete all reps on one side, then switch to the other side. 5. Complete all reps with control before resting. Keep your core engaged for stability.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 4, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 65, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'hip_thrust', 'Elevated Single Leg Hip Thrust', 'glute_bridge, romanian_deadlift, leg_curl', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1382a7ad-d896-4068-9913-486ea6e5f586', 'Spider Crawl Push Up', 'Chest', 'Bodyweight', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'The Spider Crawl Push Up is a lower body pushing exercise that targets your chest. You''ll also feel your triceps, front delts working to support the movement. This bodyweight exercise requires no equipment and can be done anywhere. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '34371201', '34371201-Spider-Crawl-Push-up-(female)_Hips.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:38.153182+00', '1. Keep your body in a straight line from head to heels throughout. 2. Lower your chest toward the floor by bending your elbows. 3. Push through your palms to return to the starting position. 4. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Keep the movement smooth and controlled. An effective movement for your legs routine.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 2, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'push_up', 'Spider Crawl Push Up', 'bench_press, chest_fly, dip', TRUE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('13844900-39ae-496e-9158-e536feadf1a9', 'Deep Squat Turn Knee Tap', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Deep Squat Turn Knee Tap provides a deep stretch for your quads, ideal for recovery and mobility work. The glutes, hamstrings assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. Regular stretching improves flexibility, reduces injury risk, and aids recovery.', '85731201', '85731201-Deep-Squat-Turn-Knee-Tap-(male)_Stretching_.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:28.52454+00', '1. Push your hips back and bend your knees to lower your body. 2. Keep your chest up and knees tracking over your toes. 3. Drive through your heels to stand back up, squeezing your glutes at the top. Ensure full range of motion on each rep. An effective movement for your stretching routine.', 'Squat', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 85, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'squat', 'Deep Squat Turn Knee Tap', 'leg_press, front_squat, goblet_squat, lunge, leg_extension', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('138aed95-13e5-40d1-b519-8438104703d7', 'Step Up On Stepbox (Step Platform)', 'Legs', 'Step Platform', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'The Bodyweight Step Up On Stepbox is a stepping exercise that primarily loads your quadriceps. Secondary activation of your glutes, hamstrings provides additional muscle engagement. Lower body strength improves everything from walking to heavy compound lifts.', '57531201', '57531201-Bodyweight-Step-up-on-Stepbox-(female)_Thighs_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:31.60311+00', '1. Set up a box or step platform at the appropriate height. 2. Step one foot onto the elevated surface. 3. Drive through that foot to lift your body up onto the platform. 4. Step back down with control and repeat. 5. Repeat for the prescribed number of repetitions. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Strength', 70, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'step_up', 'Step Up On Stepbox', 'lunge, split_squat, squat', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('1396db69-0f7e-42b5-861f-286f84b4477a', 'Side Jump Twist', 'Legs', 'Bodyweight', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Calves"}'::text[], 'A challenging plyometric exercise, the Side Jump Twist builds reactive power and improves conditioning. Your abs work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. A versatile bodyweight movement perfect for home or gym training. Develops fast-twitch muscle fibers for quicker, more powerful movements.', '50831201', '50831201-Side-Jump-Twist-(female)_Plyometrics_.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:36.985772+00', '1. Rotate your torso through the movement pattern for Side Jump Twist. 2. Control the rotation in both directions—avoid using momentum. 3. Complete all reps with control before resting.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 3, NULL, 5, 4, NULL, 8, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 7, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Plyometrics', 50, 9, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'russian_twist', 'Side Jump Twist', 'squat, bench_press, deadlift', FALSE, 'bodyweight', FALSE, 3, 60, 4, 70, 88, 95, 65),
('13a14378-34b6-4bb0-ac7d-cd1c14e4a752', 'Chest Press (Machine)', 'Chest', 'Machine', '{"Chest"}'::text[], '{"Triceps","Front Delts"}'::text[], 'Target your chest with the Lever Chest Press, an effective pressing movement for upper body strength. The triceps, front delts assist throughout the movement, making this a well-rounded exercise. The machine guides your movement path for safer, more controlled repetitions. Chest strength improves pushing power for sports, daily tasks, and other lifts.', '23191201', '23191201-Lever-Chest-Press-(VERSION-5)_Chest.mp4', 'male', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:29.971345+00', '1. Adjust the machine settings (seat height, weight, pads) to fit your body for Lever Chest Press. 2. Lower the weight toward your chest with control. 3. Press the weight up until your arms are extended (don''t lock elbows). 4. Complete all reps with control before resting. Maintain a neutral spine throughout. Include this in your chest training. Variation: Lever Chest Press.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 7, 7, NULL, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 8, 12, NULL, 6, NULL, FALSE, NULL, 'Strength', 78, 7, 8, TRUE, TRUE, 'bench_press', 'Lever Chest Press', 'incline_press, decline_press, chest_fly, push_up, dip', FALSE, 'machine', FALSE, 3, 90, 4, 80, 75, 20, 88),
('13b04d7d-5724-4361-b99f-c71fce7ca3e2', 'Low Lunge To Hamstring Stretch (Gymnastic Rings)', 'Legs', 'Gymnastic Rings', '{"Quads"}'::text[], '{"Glutes","Hamstrings"}'::text[], 'Designed to lengthen your hamstrings, the Low Lunge To Hamstring Stretch helps improve mobility and prevent stiffness. Your lower back work as secondary movers, adding to the training stimulus. Flexibility work like this enhances performance and prevents stiffness.', '77681201', '77681201-Low-Lunge-to-Hamstring-Stretch-(female)_Stretching.mp4', 'female', FALSE, '2025-12-03 23:26:35.010404+00', '1. Step forward into a lunge until both knees are at about 90 degrees. 2. Push through your front/working leg to return to the starting position. 3. Move into the stretch position for Low Lunge To Hamstring Stretch. 4. Ease into the stretch until you feel gentle tension (not pain). 5. Hold for 20-30 seconds, breathing deeply and relaxing into the stretch. Focus on maintaining proper breathing throughout.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 3, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 1, 1, NULL, 1, NULL, TRUE, NULL, 'Stretch', 48, 2, 6, FALSE, TRUE, 'hamstring_stretch', 'Low Lunge To Hamstring Stretch', 'squat, split_squat, step_up, leg_press', FALSE, 'gymnastic_rings', TRUE, 1, 30, 2, 68, 85, 85, 70);
